\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  rise on French election relief\b0\par\par\uc2 887 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2017\par 09:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     * Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rise on Emmanuel Macron's victory in\par French elections\par     * Indian rupee is the top gainer on surging domestic\par equities\par     * China's yuan is likely to appreciate in the next 2-3\par months- analyst\par     * South Korean won positive ahead of presidential elections\par on Tuesday\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Patturaja  Murugaboopathy \par     May 8 (Reuters) - Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  edged up on Monday as\par markets breathed a sigh of relief after centrist Emmanuel Macron\par was elected French President following a resounding victory over\par far-right Marine Le Pen, who had threatened to take France out\par of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par     The resulting bounce in risk appetite boosted Asian shares\par  by over half a percent and crude oil by more\par than 1 percent.\par     Macron's win put to bed fears of another populist upheaval\par after Britain's vote to exit the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  last year spread\par turmoil in global markets.\par     Elections were very much the focus in South Korea too, with\par the won up a touch ahead of Tuesday's presidential\par vote in which leading liberal candidate Moon Jae-in likely to\par emerge victorious.\par     Moon, the son of North Korean refugees who came to the South\par during the 1950-53 Korean War, would end nine years of\par conservative rule in Seoul if elected, a time when Pyongyang\par stepped up its nuclear and missile tests\par     The Indian rupee led the gainers in the region\par thanks to strong equity markets, in a sign foreign investors\par were returning after turning net sellers last week.\par     The Indonesian rupiah was trading flat after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's chief said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to curb strong rupiah appreciation.\par The rupiah, which climbed 2 percent this year up until\par mid-April, has lost about half a percent since then.\par     In the United States, fresh data suggested the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal\par Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  is on course for a June rate hike, but pressure on\par regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could be limited as markets are more or less\par priced in for a Fed move.\par      Friday's U.S. jobs data showed a sharp rebound in April\par that pointed to a tightening labor market.\par     "Fed rate hike for June is almost 100 percent priced in.\par Hence dollar movement can be limited against Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\par said Sean Yokota, head of Asia strategy at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Skandinaviska\par Enskilda Banken\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     \par     CHINA'S YUAN\par     \par     China's yuan was trading flat against the dollar,\par but the reaction was limited to official data showing April's\par exports data missed market expectations.\par     However, some analysts were bullish on the yuan, with the\par 10-year treasury yield < CN10YT=RR> touching the highest level\par in nearly two years on Monday in the wake of Beijing's\par stepped-up campaign to reduce leverage and ward off risks in the\par financial system. \par    "People should go long on CNH over the next two months.   \par The impact of leverage is to cool than crush the market." said\par Yokota, who expects CNH to trade at 6.82 levels in two to three\par months time. The offshore yuan was currently trading at\par 6.9030 per dollar.\par     The official data also showed China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par reserves rose in April for a third straight month which\par indicated China could afford to support the yuan to discourage\par bearish-yuan bets that might spur capital outflows.\par     \par     SOUTH KOREAN WON\par     \par     The South Korean won was up 0.14 percent against\par the dollar ahead of the presidential election on Tuesday.\par      The elections results are expected to bring some political\par certainty after former president Park Geun-hye was ousted in\par March over corruption charges.\par     "Regardless the final results, this election is viewed\par positively by investors as it is widely expected to end the\par uncertainties brought by the former President Park\u8217\'20\'19s\par impeachment." DBS said in a note.\par     Few pre-polls show liberal candidate Moon is likely to\par emerge victorious.\par     Among other things, Moon advocates a removal of the US THAAD\par missile defense system and re-engaging North Korea in talks,\par which would appease both China and its antagonistic northern\par neighbour.\par     \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par    Change on the day at                                        \par           0631 GMT                                      \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                     Latest bid  Previous day      Pct\par                                                            Move\par   Japan yen                  112.680            112.71    +0.03\par   Sing dlr                   1.403              1.4044    +0.07\par   Taiwan dlr                 30.148             30.182    +0.11\par 