\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  c.bank has been  \highlight22\uc2 intervening \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market to curb strong rupiah appreciation - deputy gov\b0\par\par\uc2 134 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2017\par 05:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, May 8 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb strong rupiah appreciation, its deputy governor Sugeng told an economic conference on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "Lately we've been keeping the rupiah from being too strong so that it doesn't hurt exports," said Sugeng, who like many Indonesians only goes by one name. "We hope this convinces investors that Indonesia is taking measured steps to improve its fundamentals."\par \par \uc2 The rupiah has gained 1.1 percent so far this year, but movement has been limited in the past few months. (Reporting by Hidayat Setiaji; Writing by Gayatri Suroyo and Fransiska Nangoy; Editing by Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-5-8T04:21:18.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170508ed58004pr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
