\par\par \b \uc2 PREVIEW-Indonesia c.bank seen holding key rate in wake of Fed decision\b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2016\par 05:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * All 23 analysts in poll see policy rate held at 4.75 pct\par \par \uc2 * BI decision due hours after U.S. Fed meeting ends\par \par \uc2 * Indonesia benchmark has been cut 6 times in 2016\par \par \uc2 * Decision due on Thursday, Dec 15, after 0700 GMT\par \par \uc2 By Gayatri Suroyo\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Dec 14 (Reuters) - \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is widely expected to keep its main policy rates on hold on Thursday, just hours after the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  concludes a meeting at which it is expected to raise U.S. interest rates.\par \par \uc2 A Fed rate hike, which would be the first in a year, could lure more capital away from emerging markets such as Indonesia.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, Southeast Asia's largest economy enjoyed relatively high inflows into its stock and bond markets, but the country is vulnerable to capital outflows.\par \par \uc2 Some funds left the country after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's surprise victory in the U.S. election in November.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BI) \uc2 to stabilise the rupiah was one main factor Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves dropped by $3.5 billion in November.\par \par \uc2 All 23 analysts in a Reuters poll expect BI to keep its benchmark interest rate on hold Thursday at 4.75 percent, where it has been since a cut in October.\par \par \uc2 "Were it not for the fact that the Fed is likely to hike interest rates... we would have pencilled in another (BI) rate cut for this Thursday," \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2 , a consultancy, said in a Dec. 9 note.\par \par \uc2 October's cut was BI's sixth this year, by a total of 150 basis points (bps), in an effort to accelerate economic growth.\par \par \uc2 But the 5.02 percent growth recorded in the third quarter, a slowdown from April-June, highlighted Indonesia's struggle to mount a solid rebound.\par \par \uc2 Last year's growth of 4.8 percent was the weakest since 2009. BI's forecast for 2016 growth is 5.0 percent, while its outlook for 2017 is 5.0-5.4 percent.\par \par \uc2 Out of seven analysts in the poll who gave forecasts for the benchmark at the end of March, four saw it remaining 4.75 percent, two projected a 25 bps cut and one predicted a quarter-percentage point hike.\par \par \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  is among those seeing BI on hold through March. Economist \uc2 Helmi Arman\uc2  said its general view is that the policy rate "is already at the end of the cutting cycle". (Editing by Richard Borsuk)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-12-17T04:34:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020161214ecce007y5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw442\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6630\pichgoal600
