\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Higher U.S. yields deepen Asia outflow worries; ringgit hit\b0\par\par\uc2 860 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2016\par 06:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Ringgit at 10-month low in onshore mkt; jumps in offshore\par mkt\par     * Malaysia c.bank says re-enforcing ringgit offshore trading\par rules\par     * Rupiah falls as foreigners sell stocks, long-term bonds\par     * Philippine peso hits 7-1/2-year low on equity outflows\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Nov 14 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and\par bonds extended losses on Monday, with Malaysia's ringgit near\par 10-month lows on growing fears that higher \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields\par on U.S. president-elect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy stance may spur\par more regional capital outflows.\par     Asian policymakers continued to pledged efforts to stabilise\par their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but investors took those comments as chances\par to cut risks of further depreciation in emerging Asia.\par     "It will start some bond outflows but I think we are more in\par the first step when investors hedge the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  risk," said Sean\par Yokota, head of Asia strategy at Scandinavian bank SEB in\par Singapore, when asked if higher U.S. yields will prompt more\par bond outflows. \par     "People will wait until after the Fed meeting in December to\par make big decisions on whether to sell the underlying bonds. If\par we get a bullish or hawkish forward guidance from the Fed, then\par that can start some bond selling," Yokota said, referring to the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy decision on Dec. 13-14.\par     The 10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yield jumped to a\par 10-month peak of 2.2 percent, reducing attractiveness of higher\par returns from bonds of emerging Asia.\par     Spot ringgit lost ground in the local market,\par tracking falls in Malaysia's stocks and bond prices\par . The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in offshore markets surged after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Saturday it would "re-enforce" existing\par rules that prohibit facilitation of offshore trading of the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     The Chinese yuan hit a six-year low on a weaker\par guidance rate by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2 ,\par reflecting broad strength in the U.S. dollar. \par     Indonesia's rupiah fell as long-term government\par bond prices slid and foreign investors sold local stocks. The\par Philippine peso slumped to 49.18 per dollar, its\par weakest since March 2009 on equity outflows.\par     The South Korean won skidded to a near five-month\par low as foreign investors cut stock holdings amid a deepening\par political crisis.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     Spot ringgit fell as much as 1.2 percent to 4.3300 per\par dollar, its weakest since Jan. 22.\par     Malaysia's government 10-year yield shot up more\par than 25 basis points to 4.074 percent, its highest since Jan.\par 20. Kuala Lumpur shares also lost nearly 1 percent.\par     By contrast, the ringgit jumped about 3 percent\par in non-deliverable forwards (NDFs) after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par comments.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  remains a\par non-internationalised \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , thus any offshore trading of\par ringgit such as ringgit NDFs, is not recognised.\par     Elsewhere in Asia, Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday said\par it is ready to curb excessive volatility in the Singapore dollar\par if necessary. \par     South Korea also said on Monday the government stood ready \par to act to stabilise financial markets in the wake of rising\par volatility. \par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah fell on bond outflows with the Indonesian\par government 10-year yield at 7.708 percent, the\par highest since June 27. Jakarta stocks lost nearly 3\par percent.\par     Foreign investors were net sellers in Indonesia's stock\par market over the previous three straight sessions with Friday's\par sale of 2.5 trillion rupiah ($187.3 million) being the largest\par daily unloading since Oct. 26 last year, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thomson\par Reuters\f28 \uc2 \f2  data.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem the\par rupiah's weakness on Monday, traders said, but caution increased\par over the possibility it would step in to manage volatility.\par     The authority may do so if the rupiah weakens to 13,400 per\par dollar, compared with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's session low of 13,375, a\par Jakarta-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader said.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0455 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                 Latest bid   Previous day   Pct Move\par   Japan yen                   107.40         106.69      -0.66\par   Sing dlr                    1.4141         1.4136      -0.04\par   Taiwan dlr                  31.