\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia yield-hunting back on dovish Fed; won, rupiah near 2-wk peaks\b0\par\par\uc2 837 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 September 2016\par 06:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Won jumps on stop-loss dlr selling; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspected\par     * Rupiah near 2-wk high; \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  c.bank seen cutting rates\par     * Ringgit over 1-wk peak on strong oil, Malaysia govt bonds\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Sept 22 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rallied on Thursday after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par left interest rates on hold and slowed the pace of further\par hikes, encouraging investors to seek higher yields in the\par region.\par     South Korea's won jumped to its strongest level\par in almost two weeks on stop-loss dollar selling. It gave up some\par of those gains as official \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was suspected after a\par warning against further appreciation. \par     The Indonesian rupiah also hit a near two-week high\par as local stocks and bonds rose with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expected to\par cut interest rates later in the day. \par     Malaysia's ringgit advanced to its strongest level\par in more than a week as higher crude prices eased concerns over\par the country's oil and gas revenue.\par     The Fed on Wednesday suggested it could raise rates by\par year-end if the labour market improved further, but cut the\par number of rate increases expected in 2017 and 2018. It also\par reduced its longer-run interest rate forecast to 2.9 percent\par from 3 percent. \par     That boosted risk sentiment, lifting Asian stocks and bonds.\par     "The Fed was more dovish than the market expected," said Qi\par Gao, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for Scotiabank in Singapore.\par     "EM Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will benefit from global excess\par liquidity chasing higher returns, domestic reflationary policies\par and improved market sentiment," he said. \par     The won and the ringgit will lead regional gains as the\par South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is more sensitive to risk sentiment and\par the Malaysian unit is tracking oil prices, Gao said.\par         \par     WON\par     The won jumped as much as 1.8 percent to 1,100.5 per dollar,\par its strongest since Sept. 9, on expectations of rising demand\par from exporters for settlements.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , emerging Asia's best performer\par this year, pared some gains as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were\par suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem further appreciation, traders\par said. The authorities were spotted around 1,101, they added.\par     That came as the finance ministry said it will adopt\par "appropriate responses" to prevent one-sided moves in domestic\par financial markets. \par     "If exporters accelerate unloading dollars, the won may\par strengthen to around 1,080. But it may be locked in a range\par between 1,080 and 1,120, given the authorities' focus on\par reducing volatilities," said a South Korean bank trader in\par Seoul.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah rose 0.5 percent to 13,075 per dollar, its\par strongest since Sept. 9.\par     Indonesia's shares advanced nearly 1 percent after\par foreign investors on Wednesday were net buyers of local equities\par following nine straight sessions of selling.\par     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may try to strengthen past the\par previous high of 13,055, analysts said.\par     Still, caution grew over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's strength, especially around\par 13,070-13,080, traders said.\par     "A potential rate cut could attract more bond inflows, but\par the 13,070-80 is the most BI will tolerate," said a\par Jakarta-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader, referring to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit gained as much as 0.9 percent to 4.0970 per\par dollar, its strongest since Sept. 13.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  found further support as government\par bond prices rose.\par     The ringgit is seen trying to break through a chart\par resistance at a 200-day moving average of 4.0899 with the\par previous technical resistance area of 4.1200-4.1300 becoming a\par supporting zone, analysts said.\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0445 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                  Latest bid   Previous day  Pct Move\par   Japan yen                    100.30         100.33     +0.02\par   Sing dlr                     1.3532         1.3540     +0.06\par   Taiwan dlr                   31.400         31.430     +0.10\par   Korean won                  1103.30        1120.10     +1.52\par   Baht                          34.65          34.75     +0.29\par   Peso                         4