\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Doubts on oil rebound, soft yuan hurt Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; won at 5-1/2-yr low\b0\par\par\uc2 793 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2016\par 07:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan down on strong dollar demand, weak midpoint\par     * Won falls on outflows; suspected Korea \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  limits\par     * Rupiah slides, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  c.bank seen cutting rates\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Feb 17 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par slid on Wednesday with South Korea's won at a 5-1/2-year low on\par some doubts over sustainability of an oil rebound, while a\par weaker Chinese yuan further hurt sentiment on regional units.\par     The yuan slid on increasing dollar demand after\par the long Lunar New Year holiday in China and after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set its daily guidance rate weaker again. \par     The Malaysian ringgit tracked the yuan's weakness,\par which contributed to traders dumping bullish bets on the\par second-best performing emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  this year.\par     Indonesia's rupiah fell as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par expected to cut its policy interest rate on Thursday.\par  \par     The won slid as offshore funds kept dumping it\par after recent bond sales.\par     A top \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  official cemented expectations of slow\par U.S. interest rate hikes, but that failed to support emerging\par Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Boston Fed President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Eric Rosengren\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should be "unhurried" as it considers when to again raise\par interest rates given problems overseas and financial market\par volatility that will likely dampen already low U.S. inflation.\par  \par     Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  have been pricing in views that\par the Fed may not rush to raise borrowing costs, analysts said.\par     "Almost all of what we heard from Fed policymakers in the\par past two weeks has been dovish," said \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christopher Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2 , senior\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst for Maybank in Singapore.\par     "There are other factors to look out for including ongoing\par oil talks. I think the hurdle is very high for Iran to agree to\par freeze production at January level."\par     Wong expected softer emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , in\par particular the won and the Singapore dollar.\par     Crude oil futures rebounded on Wednesday in Asia on hopes\par that a deal between Saudi Arabia and Russia to freeze oil output\par at January levels would lead to a wider pact among producers\par that could eventually see production cuts to support prices.\par  \par         \par     WON\par     The won lost nearly 1 percent to 1,228.4 per dollar, its\par weakest since July 2010.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some of the losses as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities were suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par stem a further slide for the worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par this year, traders said.\par     Song In-chang, deputy finance minister in charge of\par international finance affairs, said the country will take firm\par action when needed to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par  \par     Despite the warning and suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , foreign\par banks continued to sell the won, traders said.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is seen weakening to 1,233.2, the 38.2 percent\par Fibonacci retracement of its appreciation from 2009 to 2014,\par analysts said.\par     South Korea's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bank deposits fell for a\par third consecutive month in January to a near two-year low,\par indicating support for the won could weaken. \par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah slid as most Indonesian government bond prices\par  fell.\par     On Thursday, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  is predicted to make its second\par rate cut this year as it tries to boost sluggish growth in\par Southeast Asia's largest economy. \par     Local importers bought dollars for payments, putting further\par pressure on the rupiah.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate,\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in 2013 to manage exchange\par rate fluctuations, was fixed at 13,504, weaker than the previous\par 13,333.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0600 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       113.86         114.10       +0.21\par   Sing dlr        1.4067         1.4056       -0.08\par   Taiwan dlr      33.260         33.453       +0.58\par   Korean won     1226.24        1