\par\par \b \uc2 Jakarta Explosions, Shootout Leave at Least One Person Dead, Witnesses Say -- 2nd Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ben Otto and Resty Woro Yuniar   \par \uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2016\par 06:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Indonesia--At least one person was killed in multiple explosions and a shootout in downtown Jakarta on Thursday, witnesses said.\par \par \uc2 Witnesses said they saw at least six explosions, including blasts at a police station and a nearby \uc2 Starbucks\uc2  cafe, near the Sarinah shopping mall. One police officer was killed, witnesses said.\par \par \uc2 They said they heard gunfire as well, and saw a man shoot a police officer near the intersection between the mall and the \uc2 Starbucks\uc2 . It was unclear whether that officer was killed.\par \par \uc2 Police confirmed those explosions but declined to provide further details. Images on television showed smoke emanating from buildings in the area.\par \par \uc2 Local media said other explosions occurred near the embassies of Pakistan and Turkey several kilometers away.\par \par \uc2 Local TV said the police had cleared the area from the shopping mall to the nearby Presidential Palace.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark Jakarta stock index was recently down 1.7%.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's rupiah fell against the U.S. dollar as much as 1.0% but appeared to be stabilizing. A \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said it seemed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  through state-owned banks to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The rupiah was recently at 13,950 to the dollar compared with its Wednesday close of 13,820.\par \par \uc2 --Ewen Chew contributed to this article\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow 