\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -China market stabilisation efforts save Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  for now\b0\par\par\uc2 789 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2016\par 06:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan gains with c.bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  suspected\par     * Rupiah up on inflows ahead of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bond auction\par     * Ringgit rises on stocks, leveraged funds\par     * Won turns up; S.Korea to take actions if needed\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Jan 5 (Reuters) - Most emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par rebounded on Tuesday as China took steps to restore calm,\par including through suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , after\par a plunge in China's share markets the previous day forced\par emerging market investors into retreat.\par     Strong doubts remained over how long the uneasy calm would\par last, as there are mounting concerns over the economic slowdown.\par     "I still see downside risks from China where growth is\par slowing with no prospect of stabilisation in the manufacturing\par sector. More importantly, the CNY and CNH have weakened to\par levels, not anticipated by many - too much, too fast," said\par Nordea Markets' senior analyst Amy Yuan Zhuang in Singapore,\par referring to onshore and offshore yuan.\par     "The key question, which is hard to predict at the moment\par with vague political signal, is whether Beijing will continue\par weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . If so, then Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could feel the\par pressure."\par     The onshore Chinese yuan rose on Tuesday as the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set its daily guidance rate slightly firmer than\par many had expected. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authority was also\par suspected of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  through state-run banks to support the\par renminbi, traders said. \par     To further aid sentiment, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par injected 130 billion yuan ($19.9 billion) into money markets - \par the largest daily liquidity injection since Sept. 8.\par  \par     Those measures helped both mainland China stocks and other\par riskier assets in Asia, bolstering some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the\par region.\par     Indonesia's rupiah led gains, with inflows seen \par ahead of a government bond sale later in the day. Malaysia's\par ringgit rose on higher local stocks.\par     The South Korean won turned higher on growing\par caution over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par authorities.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah started the day weaker but turned firmer as\par Jakarta stocks jumped more than 1 percent, outperforming\par regional peers.\par     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  extended gains on capital inflows\par ahead of the government's bond auction with an indicative target\par of 12 trillion rupiah ($868.6 million) later in the day.\par     A \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader in Jakarta said the government could sell\par as much as 18 trillion rupiah.\par     Easing inflation and a shrinking current account deficit\par have recently drawn foreign investors to seek higher yields from\par Indonesia's bonds. In December, the annual inflation rate cooled\par to the lowest in six years. \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit rose as Malaysian equities also advanced over 1\par percent.\par     Leveraged funds bought the Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par non-deliverable forwards markets.\par     The ringgit also found support from demand against the\par neighbouring Singapore dollar.\par     \par     WON\par     The won earlier skidded to 1,192.1 per dollar, its weakest\par since Sept. 30, tracking weakness in the offshore yuan.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reversed initial losses as the\par onshore renminbi rose on suspected \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \par     Caution also grew over possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by South Korea\par as the authorities were on Monday spotted in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par to stem the won's weakness.\par     "A turnaround in Chinese markets and suspected dollar\par supplies from the authorities caused stop-loss dollar selling,"\par said a South Korean bank trader in Seoul.\par     A senor \f28 \uc2 \f2 South Korean finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  official said on\par Tuesday the government will take action to stabilise markets if\par needed. \par         \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0500 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.52         119.46       -0.05\par   Sing dlr        1.4237         1.4248       +0.08\par   Taiwan dlr      33.061         33.236       +0.53\par   Korean won     1185.50        1187.70  