\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah jumps, on course for biggest rise in 7 yrs on inflows\b0\par\par\uc2 842 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Oktober 2015\par 09:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Indonesia c.bank: rupiah should be firmer than 14,000/dlr\par     * Ringgit to post largest gain in 2 years on exports, oil\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Oct 7 - The Indonesian rupiah jumped on\par Wednesday, on track for its best daily performance in seven\par years, thanks to capital inflows as expectations of an imminent\par U.S. interest rate hike ebbed and on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par to stabilise the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Malaysia's ringgit was also poised for its largest\par daily gain in two years on stronger-than-expected August exports\par data and resurgent oil prices.\par     The rupiah rallied 2.8 percent to 13,850 per dollar\par as of 0625 GMT, which would be the largest daily rise since\par December 2008 if it sustains the gains to the closing bell. The\par Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose 1.8 percent on Tuesday, the biggest\par jump since September 2009.\par     Indonesia's government bond prices rose, led by long-term\par papers. The 10-year yield fell to 8.710 percent, its\par lowest since Aug. 20, while the 15-year yield slid\par to 8.870 percent, the lowest since Aug. 12.\par     On Tuesday, foreign investors bought a net 844.8 billion\par rupiah ($61 million) in Jakarta stocks, the largest\par daily purchase since July 10.\par     "We can certainly expect to see some inflows returning in\par the near-term, which will support the rupiah to some extent,"\par said Khoon Goh, senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for ANZ in Singapore.\par     He said sentiment improved due to waning prospects of an\par interest rate hike by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  before year-end after\par disappointing U.S. jobs data last week.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has also been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the spot market\par to prop up the second-worst performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far\par this year, traders said.\par     Earlier, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said the rupia's value\par based on fundamentals should be stronger than 14,000 per dollar.\par  \par     Last week, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced a series of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par measures such as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the forward market.\par  The one-month dollar/rupiah forwards \par plunged almost 30 percent on Wednesday.\par     The rupiah also jumped in non-deliverable forwards (NDFs)\par  on stop-loss dollar selling. The one-month NDFs\par advanced as much as 2.4 percent to 13,940 per dollar, its\par strongest since Aug. 13.\par     Indonesia will announce a third stimulus package later in\par the day aimed at supporting consumption, streamlining the\par bureaucracy and reviving economic growth, the chief economics\par minister said. \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit rose 2.2 percent, which would be the largest\par daily gain since September 2013, as traders rushed to unwind\par bearish bets in the worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this\par year.\par     Malaysia's exports in August rose 4.1 percent from a year\par earlier, beating a forecast of 2.0 percent growth in a Reuters\par poll. \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  found further support as a rebound in global\par crude prices eased concerns over the country's overseas earnings\par from oil and gas sales.\par     Scandinavian bank SEB said it will add the one-month ringgit\par NDFs holdings with a target of 4.0500 per dollar. The NDFs stood\par at 4.2500.\par     "The political headwinds have not disappeared but momentum\par has subsided," said Sean Yokota, head of Asia strategy for SEB\par in a note.\par     "Commodity price decline is also losing momentum and\par Malaysia is one of the most commodity sensitive economy due to\par its palm oil exports."\par     The ringgit has lost 18.4 percent against the dollar so far\par this year due to low commodity prices and a graft scandal\par surrounding Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Najib Razak\f28 \uc2 \f2  and indebted state-fund\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 1Malaysia Development Berhad\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0625 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.98         120.24       +0.22\par   Sing dlr        1.4187         1.4189       +0.01\par   Taiwan dlr      32.627         32.937       +0.95\par   Korean won     1159.99        1165.90       +0.51\par   Baht             35.97          36.32       +0.97\par   Peso             46.23          46.47       +0.52\par   Rupiah        13850.00       14241.00       +2.82\par   Rupee            65.26          65.41       +0.23\par   Ringgit         4.2825         4.3745       +2.15\par  *Yuan            6.3571         6.3571       +0.00\par  \par   Change so far in 2015\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par 