\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia c.bank unveils measures aimed to stabilize the rupiah\b0\par\par\uc2 469 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2015\par 11:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * C.bank says it will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in rupiah forward market\par \par \uc2 * Policy package is to 'maintain' stability - deputy gov\par \par \uc2 * BI will issue certificates in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Measure should ease short-term pressure - analysts (Adds comments, details)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Sept 30 (Reuters) - \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unveiled on Wednesday a set of measures intended to stabilize the country's beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which tumbled to its lowest levels since 1998 in the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 Key steps include the planned issuance of \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  certificates in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the forward market for rupiah, in order contain expectations on how much more it might depreciate.\par \par \uc2 The focus of the package "is to maintain rupiah stability, manage \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  liquidity, and manage supply and demand for dollars," said Perry Warjiyo, a \uc2 Bank Indonesia (BI) \uc2 deputy governor.\par \par \uc2 Saktiandi Supaat, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  research for Maybank in Singapore, said the moves could ensure greater dollar supply in the forward market to meet any increase in demand.\par \par \uc2 "Such measures could go some ways to ease pressure on the rupiah in the near term, but in the medium- to longer-terms, more far ranging reforms in the economic and financial realms are needed instead," he said.\par \par \uc2 Josua Pardede, an economist with Bank Permata in Jakarta, said the BI's measures, together with some announced earlier, are "really good to limit the rupiah depreciation, although the exchange rate would still be under pressure from U.S. rate uncertainty".\par \par \uc2 SECOND WORST PERFORMER\par \par \uc2 The rupiah is the second worst performer in emerging Asia this year, after the Malaysian ringgit. The rupiah has weakened more than 15 percent against the dollar, which the bulk of the loss coming in the third quarter.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the rupiah touched a new 17-year low of 14,730 to the dollar. On Wednesday afternoon, it was trading around 14,650.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, Warjiyo said the fundamental value of the rupiah for the rest of the year should be between 13,300-13,700 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 BI Indonesia will also reissue 3-month \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  certificates and 2-week reverse repurchase agreements.\par \par \uc2 "We want to drive (liquidity) from short-term instruments towards longer-term instruments because we're afraid excessive (liquidity) in short-term will create speculation. So we reopen these instruments," said Mirza Adityaswara, BI's senior deputy governor.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the Indonesian government announced the second instalment of its stimulus package to support economic growth, which include a deposit tax discount for exporters to keep their foreign earnings onshore. This policy will be implemented in coordination with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (Reporting by Hidayat Setiaji, Gayatri Suroyo and Fransiska Nangoy in JAKARTA and Masayuki Kitano in SINGAPORE; Editing by Richard Borsuk) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-9-30T10:47:43.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150930eb9u00bwh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
