\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Global equity market gains help Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , rupiah up on c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 790 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 August 2015\par 08:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  not through agent banks - traders\par     * Jakarta to unveil policy package to help rupiah, economy\par     * Taiwan dollar up on demand from foreigners, exporters\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 27 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par gained on Thursday as sharp rebounds in global stocks eased\par concerns there could be a protracted rout in financial markets,\par while the Indonesian rupiah rose with traders spotting direct\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The rupiah earlier hit a 17-year low, but reversed \par direction on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  found further\par support from the government's plans for a policy package to prop\par up the unit and the economy. \par     Taiwan's dollar advanced on demand from foreign\par investors and month-end corporate demand.\par     China's stocks, the centre of the recent global market\par turmoil, rose by early afternoon, helping an index of Asian\par equities enjoy a 1.6 percent gain. U.S. shares saw their largest\par one-day rise in four years.\par     Sentiment on risky assets also improved as New York Fed\par President \f28 \uc2 \f2 William Dudley\f28 \uc2 \f2  said a U.S. interest rate hike next\par month seems less appropriate given the threat posed to the\par world's largest economy by a recent financial market rout.\par  \par     Still, investors found little conviction on further rebounds\par in regional stocks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     "Improved risk sentiment and easing equity market volatility\par will support Asia ex-Japan \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  temporarily," said\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Christopher Wong\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a senior \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at Maybank in\par Singapore.\par     "Equity volatility is not over yet," said Wong, adding the\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 CBOE\f28 \uc2 \f2  Volatility index is still well above 2012-2015\par average.\par     The index, Wall Street's so-called fear gauge, on Monday hit\par its highest since January 2009, the middle of the global\par financial crisis.\par     Caution also grew ahead of an annual conference in Jackson\par Hole, Wyoming, attended by many of the world's top central\par bankers. Investors will try to seek clues on when the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal\par Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  would start raising interest rates.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah earlier slid to 14,135 per dollar, its weakest\par since July 1998.\par     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  turned firmer as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia (BI)\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 was spotted directly selling dollars, not though agent banks, to\par lift the rupiah, traders said.\par     The unusual move indicated strong determination of the\par authority to support the second-worst performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par so far this year, traders said.\par     "BI wants to show the market their presence. It is a crucial\par and very rare event," said a Jakarta-based \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader.\par     Usually, central banks use other banks such as state-run\par lenders for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The rupiah hit a session high of 14,020 after the government\par said it will unveil a policy package Thursday afternoon to\par support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the economy. Jakarta shares \par were up more than 3 percent.\par     \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par     The Taiwan dollar advanced on demand from foreign\par institutional investors with local stocks up 1.4\par percent.\par     The island's exporters bought the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for month-end\par settlements.\par     \par     WON\par     South Korea's won rose on month-end demand from\par exporters. Traders continued to cover short positions on a\par recovery in China's stocks.\par     Foreign investors, however, continued to dump Seoul shares\par , limiting the won's upside.\par     They were net sellers in the main stock market for a 16th\par straight session and have unloaded a net 4.1 trillion won ($3.5\par billion) during the period, Korea Exchange data showed.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0610 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       119.86         119.95       +0.08\par   Sing dlr        1.4030         1.4059       +0.21\par   Taiwan dlr      32.360         32.765       +1.25\par   Korean won     1184.76        1186.00       +0.10\par   Baht             35.66          35.64       -0.06\par   Peso             46.77          46.72       -0.10\par   Rupiah        14060.00       14120.00       +0.43\par   Rupee            66.09          66.14       +0.08\par   Ringgit         4.2520         4.2520       +0.00\par   Yuan      