\par\par \b \uc2 *\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  Gov: Market Turmoil 'Temporary'\b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2015\par 08:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 26 Aug 2015 02:15 ET *\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  Gov: Market Turmoil May Last Until March\par \par \uc2 26 Aug 2015 02:16 ET *\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  Gov: Funds Will Return to Emerging Markets With Good Prospects\par \par \uc2 26 Aug 2015 02:16 ET *\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  Gov: Indonesian Economy 'Far From Being in Crisis'\par \par \uc2 26 Aug 2015 03:16 ET  \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  Gov: Market Turmoil 'Temporary'\par \par \uc2 By I Made Sentana\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA--The global financial market turmoil is likely "temporary" and will last until around March next year, Bank Indonesia Gov. Agus Martowardojo said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Martowardojo said once the market settles down funds will flow back to emerging economies that have good prospects and Indonesia will be among those that will appear on investors' radar.\par \par \uc2 "Indonesia's economic fundamentals are actually improving as inflation and current-account deficit is easing," he added.\par \par \uc2 Asian markets struggled to shake a global selloff Wednesday, as worries about whether \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had done enough to spur its slowing economy sent Shanghai into another volatile session. While some stock markets in the region rebounded, trading in China's main index remained rocky, with Shanghai rising as much as 1% but also falling nearly 4%.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said although Indonesia's economic growth has slowed to its lowest level in six years at 4.7% year-over-year each in the first and second quarters of the year from an average of 5.4% in every quarter in the past six years, the pace was still better than in many countries.\par \par \uc2 "I want to repeat again that Indonesia is far away from being in a crisis. But we have to remain careful," Mr. Martowardojo said.\par \par \uc2 He stated that \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and will continue to do so in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep the rupiah volatility in a "healthy range."\par \par \uc2 The dollar Wednesday rose to fresh 17-year high of 14,155 rupiah Wednesday, which prompted \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  to sell dollars again, traders said\par \par \uc2 Write to I Made Sentana at I-made.sentana@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 August 26, 2015 03:16 ET (07:16 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150826eb8q000dr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
