\par\par \b \uc2 Rupiah Slides Despite Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 August 2015\par 06:57\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0434 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is suspected to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market today as the rupiah continues sliding to fresh 17-year lows on regional markets' muted reaction to China's latest round of monetary stimulus. Three traders in Jakarta say they spotted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling $100 million so far when the pair was quoted at IDR14,100. "This doesn't seem to be much compared with the daily amount of dollars they sold in the market in the past few days of around $300 million on average per day because some banks also started to sell dollars this morning," a trader says. She adds some banks sold dollars likely on behalf of exporters who need the rupiah to pay taxes or salaries. Bank Indonesia deputy governor Perry Warjiyo said Tuesday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market lately. \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said the rupiah has been undervalued.\par \par \uc2  Yet, traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not expected to try to reverse the USD/IDR movement as such a move will deplete its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, which could further hurt the rupiah. (i-made.sentana@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Editor: KLH\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 26-08-15 0457GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020150826eb8q0005t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscale