\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  haunted as China devaluation sparks  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  war fears\b0\par\par\uc2 1,042 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 09:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Yuan hits 4-year low after \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  sets weaker midpoint\par     * Ringgit below 4/dollar, rupiah at fresh 17-year trough\par     * Singapore dlr, Taiwan dlr, Philippine peso at 5-year lows\par     * Vietnam doubles \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading band to 2 pct\par \par  (Adds more details. Updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, Aug 12 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell\par to multi-year lows on Wednesday after \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par allowed the yuan to drop for the second straight day to a\par four-year trough, a move sparking fears of a global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par war.\par     The yuan fell to as low as 6.4508 per dollar, its\par lowest since July 2011, after the \f28 \uc2 \f2 People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par weakened its daily yuan midpoint by 1.6 percent. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2 , which described the devaluation\par as a one-off step to make the yuan more responsive to market\par forces, sought to reassure financial markets it was not\par embarking on a steady depreciation. \par     But markets stayed jittery, expecting the move could be the\par start of a further slide and driving the yuan's peers weaker,\par analysts said.\par     China took steps to weaken the yuan after disappointing\par economic data indicated that further stimulus may be needed to\par revive growth in the world's second-largest economy. China's\par July factory output rose 6.0 percent from a year earlier, well\par below market expectations. \par     "It wasn't meant to be one-off for sure and there will be\par further depreciation until the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  stabilises the spot to\par re-align with the fixing, which requires more significant\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  effort," said Andy Ji, Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist\par for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commonwealth Bank of Australia\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore.\par     In the meantime, Ji added, the U.S. dollar "will march on",\par strengthening further against Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     Malaysia's ringgit weakened past a psychologically\par important 4.0000 per dollar level to hit a fresh 17-year pre-peg\par low. Indonesia's rupiah also fell to a level not seen\par since July 1998.\par     The Singapore dollar, the Taiwan dollar \par and the Philippine peso all touched five-year\par troughs.\par     The South Korea won slid to nearly a four-year\par low.\par     China's devaluation bolstered expectations that other Asian\par countries may let their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weaken to support their\par economies, as long as the pace of depreciation is not too fast.\par     South Korea's finance minister said China's step to weaken\par the yuan will help South Korean exports eventually.\par  \par     Vietnam doubled its trading band for interbank dollar/dong\par transactions on Wednesday, aiming to protect its exports by\par countering the adverse affects of a strengthening dollar and\par yuan devaluation. \par     Some \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities in Asia, including South\par Korea and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , were spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to defend their\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but it does not indicate they favour stronger\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , analysts said.\par     "They need to slow down speed as excessive volatilities\par could spur massive capital outflows," said Yuna Park, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par and bond analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Seoul.\par     "No one wants appreciation in this \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  war. A slow\par depreciation is the best."\par         \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah lost as much as 1.7 percent to 13,825 per dollar,\par its weakest since July 1998, as Jakarta shares dropped\par 3.2 percent earlier.\par     Foreigners' hedging-related dollar demand hurt the rupiah\par further, traders said.\par     The Indonesian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some losses as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted "heavily" \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief said the rupiah's decline has overshot\par and it is undervalued, after a senior deputy governor warned of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit dropped 1.8 percent to 4.0320 per dollar, its\par weakest since Sept. 1, 1998.\par     Malaysia pegged the ringgit at 3.8000 from early September\par 1998 to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  during the Asian financial crisis.\par The country took the ringgit off the peg in 2005.\par     Kuala Lumpur stocks lost 1.9 percent amid sliding\par investor confidence due to falling commodity prices and growing\par pressure on Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Najib Razak\f28 \uc2 \f2  amid corruption\par allegations involving indebted state fund \f28 \uc2 \f2 1Malaysia Development\par Berhad\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     Most government bond prices fell. The five-year government\par bond yield jumped to 3.969 percent, its highest since\par November 2008.\par     \par     WON\par     The won lost as much as 1.4 percent to 1,195.5 per dollar,\par its weakest since October 2011, on dollar demand from foreign\par banks.\par     The South Korean \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pared some losses as traders in\par Seoul suspected the local authorities of selling dollars to tame\par the won's volatility.\par     \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par     The Singapore dollar fell 1.1 percent to 1.4165 to the U.S.\par dollar, its weakest since June 2010.\par     The city-state's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  closely tracks the yuan as traders\par and analysts believe it is included in the undisclosed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par basket used by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  to manage\par monetary policy.\par     Singapore's benchmark three-month interest rate rose to a\par four-month high on the weak local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as investors seek\par higher yields as compensation for holding it.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0622 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       124.85         125.13       +0.22\par   Sing dlr        1.4135         1.4014       -0.86\par   Taiwan dlr      32.201     