\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight\uc2  c.bank "heavily"  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to defend rupiah - traders\b0\par\par\uc2 151 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 07:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE/JAKARTA, Aug 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted "heavily" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the rupiah on Wednesday, traders said, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a level last seen during the Asian financial crisis 17 years ago.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah was down 1.6 percent to 13,820 per dollar as of 0450 GMT, after hitting 13,825, its weakest since July 1998.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia Senior Deputy Governor Mirza Adityaswara told Reuters earlier that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will guard the rupiah against volatility, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's depreciation does not reflect economic fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 He declined to comment further.\par \par \uc2 One trader in Jakarta said he believed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had spent no more than $400 million on Wednesday to support the rupiah. (Reporting by Jongwoo Cheon, Gayatri Suroyo and Fransiska Nangoy; Editing by Richard Borsuk) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-8-12T06:01:59.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150812eb8c0071b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
