\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia Rupiah Sinks to New Low on Fresh Yuan Weakness -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 209 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 2015\par 06:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0348 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia's rupiah dropped sharply against the U.S. dollar Wednesday after \uc2 China's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  marked the yuan weaker again and triggered another sharp yuan selloff. The rupiah fell as much as 1.5% from its Tuesday close-- nearly matching the 1.6% fall of the yuan--to hit a new 17-year low of 13,800 to the U.S. dollar. The rupiah's weakness is not that alarming when taken into context--Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have slumped across the board after Tuesday's shock devaluation of the yuan by the \uc2 People's Bank of China\uc2 , and Malaysia's ringgit is also at a 17-year low to the greenback. While \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tuesday that the rupiah is undervalued--which raises concerns of imported inflation and capital outflows--there doesn't appear to be aggressive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the rupiah's decline, perhaps because it helps exporters. The rupiah, now at 13,800 from its Tuesday close of 13,595, has depreciated 10.3% against the U.S. dollar this year.\par \par \uc2  (ewen.chew@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 Editor JSM\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 12-08-15 0416GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020150812eb8c0005s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
