                                                               such determination, the "Rate Fixing \par                                                                 Date" shall be the date that is five (5) IDR Business \par                                                                 Days prior to the date upon which the \par                                                                 Notes become due and payable as provided in Condition \par                                                                 9 (Default). \par  20.   Governing Law:                                           New York \par  21.   Selling Restrictions: \par         (a) United States:                                       Under the provisions of Section 11(a) of the \par                                                                  \f28 \uc2 \f2 Inter-American Development Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Act, the Notes \par                                                                  are exempted securities within the meaning of Section \par                                                                  3(a)(2) of the U.S. Securities Act of \par                                                                  1933, as amended, and Section 3(a)(12) of the U.S. \par                                                                  Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as amended. \par        (b) United Kingdom:                                      The Dealer represents and agrees that it has complied \par                                                                 and will comply with all applicable \par                                                                 provisions of the Financial Services and Markets Act \par                                                                 2000 with respect to anything done by \par                                                                 it in relation to the Notes in, from or otherwise \par                                                                 involving the United Kingdom. \par        (c) Indonesia:                                           The Notes are not and will not be registered with the \par                                                                 Financial Services Authority previously \par                                                                 known as the Capital Market and Financial Institutions \par                                                                 Supervisory Agency (the "OJK") in Indonesia. \par                                                                 As such, the Notes (including the distribution and \par                                                                 dissemination of the Pricing Supplement, \par                                                                 other written materials either through advertisements \par                                                                 or other media authorized) are not authorized \par                                                                 by the OJK for their sale by public offering in the \par                                                                 Indonesian territory and/or to Indonesian \par                                                                 entities or residents in the Indonesian territory in \par                                                                 circumstances which constitute a public \par                                                                 offering of securities under the Indonesian Law No. \par                                                                 8/1995 regarding Capital Markets. Likewise, \par                                                                 the Notes and the Pricing Supplement have not been \par                                                                 reviewed, registered or authorized by the \par                                                                 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (\f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 ) for their distribution \par                                                                 through banking institutions in Indonesia. \par        (d) General:                                             No action has been or will be taken by the Issuer that \par                                                                 would permit a public offering of the \par                                                                 Notes, or possession or distribution of any offering \par                                                                 material relating to the Notes in any \par                                                                 jurisdiction where action for that purpose is \par                                                                 required. Accordingly, the Dealer agrees that \par                                                                 it will observe all applicable provisions of law in \par                                                                 each jurisdiction in or from which it \par                                                                 may offer or sell Notes or distribute any offering \par                                                                 material. \par  Other Relevant Terms \par  1.    Listing:                                                 Application has been made for the Notes to be admitted \par                                                                 to the Official List of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 United \par                                                                 Kingdom Listing Authority\f28 \uc2 \f2  and to trading on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London \par                                                                 Stock Exchange plc\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Regulated Market \par                                                                 with effect from the Issue Date. \par  2.    Details of Clearance System Approved by the Bank and \par        the \par        Global Agent and Clearance and \par        Settlement Procedures:                                    \f28 \uc2 \f2 Euroclear Bank SA/NV\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Clearstream\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Luxembourg \par  3.    Syndicated:                                              No. \par  4.    Commissions and Concessions:                             None. \par  5.    Estimated Total Expenses:                                None. The Dealer has agreed to pay for all material \par                                                                 expenses related to the issuance of the \par                                                                 Notes. \par  6.    Codes: \par        (a) ISIN:                                                XS1241559324 \par        (b) Common Code:                                         124155932 \par  7.    Identity of Dealer:                                      \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup Global Markets Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par  8.    Identity of Calculation Agent:                           \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citibank, N.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., London office - EM Derivatives \par                                                                 Calculations \par  \par                                                                 In relation to the Rate Fixing Date, as soon as is \par                                                                 reasonably practicable after the determination \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 24-06-15 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                                                 of the IDR Rate in relation thereto, on the date on \par                                                                 which the relevant IDR Rate is to be determined \par                                                                 (or, if such date is not a Relevant Business Day, then \par                                                                 on the next succeeding Relevant Business \par                                                                 Day), the Calculation Agent shall notify the Issuer \par                                                                 and the Global Agent of the IDR Rate, \par                                                                 and the Interest Amount, and the Redemption Amount or \par                                                                 Early Redemption Amount, as the case \par                                                                 may be, in relation thereto. \par                                                                 All determinations of the Calculation Agent shall (in \par                                                                 the absence of manifest error) be final \par                                                                 and binding on all parties (including, but not limited \par                                                                 to, the Bank and the Noteholders) and \par                                                                 shall be made in its sole discretion in good faith and \par                                                                 in a commercially reasonable manner \par                                                                 in accordance with a calculation agent agreement \par                                                                 between the Bank and the Calculation Agent. \par  9.    Provision for Registered Notes: \par        (a) Individual Definitive Registered Notes Available \par        on Issue Date:                                            No \par        (b) DTC Global Note(s):                                  No \par        (c) Other Registered Global Notes:                       Yes, issued in accordance with the Global Agency \par                                                                 Agreement, dated January 8, 2001, among the \par                                                                 Bank, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citibank, N.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., as Global Agent, and the other \par                                                                 parties thereto. \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Additional Information regarding the Notes\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1. The EU has adopted a Directive regarding the taxation of savings income (the "Savings Directive"). The Savings Directive requires Member States (as defined below) to provide to the tax authorities of other Member States details of payments of interest and other similar income paid by a person to an individual in another Member State, except that Austria will instead impose a withholding system for a transitional period unless during such period it elects otherwise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank undertakes that it will ensure that it maintains a paying agent in a country which is a member of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  (a "Member State") that will not be obliged to withhold or deduct tax pursuant to the Savings Directive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    2.         United States Federal Tax Matters \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following supplements the discussion under the "Tax Matters" section of the Prospectus regarding the U.S. federal income tax treatment of the Notes, and is subject to the limitations and exceptions set forth therein. Any tax disclosure in the Prospectus or this pricing supplement is of a general nature only, is not exhaustive of all possible tax considerations and is not intended to be, and should not be construed to be, legal, business or tax advice to any particular prospective investor. Each prospective investor should consult its own tax advisor as to the particular tax consequences to it of the acquisition, ownership, and disposition of the Notes, including the effects of applicable U.S. federal, state, and local tax laws and non-U.S. tax laws and possible changes in tax laws.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Due to a change in law since the date of the Prospectus, the second paragraph of "-Payments of Interest" under the "United States Holders" section should be updated to read as follows: "Interest paid by the Bank on the Notes constitutes income from sources outside the United States and will, depending on the circumstances, be "passive" or "general" income for purposes of computing the foreign tax credit."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Because the Notes are denominated in the Indonesian Rupiah, a United States holder of the Notes will generally be subject to special United States federal income tax rules governing foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions, as described in the Prospectus in the last four paragraphs of "-Payments of Interest" under the "United States Holders" section. We believe that a United States holder will be required to determine amounts received with respect to a Note (including principal and interest) by reference to the U.S. dollar value of the Indonesian Rupiah amount of the payment, calculated at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rate in effect on the date of payment. The U.S. dollar amount that is actually received by the United States holder may differ from the amount determined under the preceding sentence, since the U.S. dollar amount of the payment will be determined by reference to the IDR Rate as of the relevant Rate Fixing Date. Accordingly, a United States holder of the Notes may recognize United States source foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain or loss in an amount equal to such difference (in addition to any foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gain or loss otherwise recognized upon the receipt of an interest payment or a sale or retirement of the Notes). The \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Internal Revenue Service\f28 \uc2 \f2  could take the position, however, that the amounts received by a United States holder in respect of a Note should be equal to the U.S. dollar amount that is actually received by the United States holder. Prospective United States holders of the Notes should consult their tax advisors regarding these rules.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Treasury Regulations Requiring Disclosure of Reportable Transactions.Treasury regulations require United States taxpayers to report certain transactions that give rise to a loss in excess of certain thresholds (a "Reportable Transaction"). Under these regulations, because the Notes are denominated in a foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a United States holder that recognizes a loss with respect to the Notes that is characterized as an ordinary loss due to changes in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates (under any of the rules discussed under the "Tax Matters" section of the Prospectus) would be required to report the loss on \f28 \uc2 \f2 IRS\f28 \uc2 \f2  Form 8886 (Reportable Transaction Statement) if the loss exceeds the thresholds set forth in the regulations. For individuals and trusts, this loss threshold is $50,000 in any single taxable year. For other types of taxpayers and other types of losses, the thresholds are higher. Holders should consult with their tax advisors regarding any tax filing and reporting obligations that may apply in connection with acquiring, owning and disposing of notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Information with Respect to Foreign Financial Assets. Owners of "specified foreign financial assets" with an aggregate value in excess of U.S.$50,000 (and in some circumstances, a higher threshold) may be required to file an information report with respect to such assets with their tax returns. "Specified foreign financial assets" may include financial accounts maintained by foreign financial institutions, as well as the following, but only if they are held for investment and not held in accounts maintained by financial institutions: (i) stocks and securities issued by non-United States persons, (ii) financial instruments and contracts that have non-United States issuers or counterparties, and (iii) interests in foreign entities. Holders are urged to consult their tax advisors regarding the application of this reporting requirement to their ownership of the Notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Medicare Tax. A United States holder that is an individual or estate, or a trust that does not fall into a special class of trusts that is exempt from such tax, is subject to a 3.8% tax (the "Medicare tax") on the lesser of (1) the United States holder's "net investment income" (or "undistributed net investment income" in the case of an estate or trust) for the relevant taxable year and (2) the excess of the United States holder's modified adjusted gross income for the taxable year over a certain threshold (which in the case of individuals is between U.S.$125,000 and U.S.$250,000, depending on the individual's circumstances). A holder's net investment income generally includes its interest income and its net gains from the disposition of Notes, unless such interest income or net gains are derived in the ordinary course of the conduct of a trade or business (other than a trade or business that consists of certain passive or trading activities). United States holders that are individuals, estates or trusts are urged to consult their tax advisors regarding the applicability of the Medicare tax to their income and gains in respect of their investment in the Notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    3.         Additional Investment Considerations: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Notes offered by this Pricing Supplement are complex financial instruments and may not be suitable for certain investors. Investors intending to purchase the Notes should consult with their tax and financial advisors to ensure that the intended purchase meets the investment objective before making such purchase. [ 24-06-15 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There are various risks associated with the Notes including, but not limited to, exchange rate risk, price risk and liquidity risk. Investors should consult with their own financial, legal and accounting advisors about the risks associated with an investment in these Notes, the appropriate tools to analyze that investment, and the suitability of the investment in each investor's particular circumstances. Holders of the Notes should also consult with their professional tax advisors regarding tax laws applicable to them.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Payment of each Interest Amount and the Redemption Amount will be based on the IDR Rate, which is a measure of the rate of exchange between the Indonesian Rupiah and the USD. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates are volatile and will affect the holder's return. In addition, the government of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can from time to time \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. These \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or other governmental actions could adversely affect the value of the Notes, as well as the yield (in USD terms) on the Notes and the amount payable at maturity or upon acceleration. Even in the absence of governmental action directly affecting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates, political or economic developments in Indonesia or elsewhere could lead to significant and sudden changes in the exchange rate between the Indonesian Rupiah and the USD.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian Rupiah is an emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be subject to particularly substantial volatility, as well as to government actions including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  controls, devaluations and other matters which could materially and adversely affect the value of the Notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The methodologies for determining the IDR Rate may result in a Redemption Amount (or Early Redemption Amount, as the case may be) of the Notes, or an Interest Amount on the Notes, being significantly less than anticipated or less than what an alternative methodology for determining the IDR-USD exchange rate would yield.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 INTER-AMERICAN DEVELOPMENT BANK\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Name:   \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gustavo Alberto De Rosa\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par    Title:      Chief Financial Officer and \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Manager, Finance Department\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This information is provided by RNS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The company news service from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 END\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IODUOSKRVUANUAR [ 24-06-15 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument RNS0000020150624eb6o0001s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
