\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesia's  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  reserves drop to $111.6 bln at end-March\b0\par\par\uc2 94 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 April 2015\par 12:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, April 8 (Reuters) - Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell to $111.6 billion at the end of March as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement on Wednesday.               \par \par \uc2 Reserves stood at $115.53 billion at the end of February.               \par \par \uc2 The rupiah touched a 17-year low of 13,245 against the dollar in March, but it has rallied since then and traded at 12,950 on Wednesday.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-4-8T11:03:55.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150408eb4800b8d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
