\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Solid U.S. jobs hit Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 ; rupiah near 17-year low\b0\par\par\uc2 779 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 06:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Rupiah lowest since 1998 on stocks, bonds, corp dlr bids\par     * Ringgit hits 6-year low on sliding oil prices\par     * \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Malaysia c.banks \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spotted\par     * Won at 3-month low on offshore funds, importers\par \par  (Adds text, updates prices)\par     By Jongwoo Cheon\par     SINGAPORE, March 9 (Reuters) - Emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par lost ground on Monday after stronger-than-expected U.S. job data\par boosted expectations that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  may raise interest\par rates in the middle of this year, hurting regional\par attractiveness of higher yields.\par     Adding to depreciation pressure, China's imports in the\par first two months of the year fell more than 20 percent from a\par year earlier, indicating persistent weakness in the world's\par second-largest economy. \par     The Indonesian rupiah hit a near 17-year trough as\par bonds and stocks slid. The Malaysian ringgit touched a\par six-year low, while the Singapore dollar stayed around\par its weakest since July 2010.\par     South Korea's won slid to a three-month low as\par offshore funds sold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     U.S. nonfarm payrolls rose 295,000 in February, beating a\par market forecast for a 240,000 increase, data showed on Friday.\par The jobless rate last month fell to 5.5 percent, the lowest\par level since May 2008. \par     Those healthy numbers sent the dollar to a fresh\par 11-year high against a six major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and lifted \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S.\par Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  bond yields.\par     "The strong jobs data helped the 10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yield\par rise above 2.2 percent despite lower oil prices. That indicated\par markets were pricing in an earlier interest rate hike," said\par Yuna Park, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and bond analyst at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dongbu Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2  in\par Seoul.\par     "The dollar's strength and volatilities in emerging\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will intensify, especially in the second quarter,"\par Park added.\par     The benchmark U.S. note yield stood at 2.2289\par percent on Monday in Asia. The yield on Friday in New York\par posted their biggest rise since November 2013.\par     \par     RUPIAH\par     The rupiah lost 0.7 percent to 13,070 per dollar, its\par weakest since August 1998, on dollar demand from local\par companies.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also slid in non-deliverable forwards\par  markets.\par     Most Indonesian government bond returns rose, with yields of\par  10-year debt and 15-year bonds at their\par highest levels since mid-February. Jakarta shares lost\par 1.3 percent, underperforming regional peers.\par     The official Jakarta Interbank Spot Dollar Rate,\par which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  introduced in 2013 to manage exchange\par rate fluctuations, was fixed at 13,047 rupiah per dollar, the\par weakest since the launch.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the\par worst-performing Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  so far this year around the\par session's low, traders said.\par     However, the authority did not seem to be defending specific\par levels, they added.\par     \par     RINGGIT\par     The ringgit fell 1.0 percent to 3.6900 per dollar, its\par weakest since March 2009.\par     The Malaysian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  came under further pressure as oil\par prices slid, underscoring concerns that falling crude will hurt\par the country's current account surplus and widen its fiscal\par deficit.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was spotted \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to support the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , traders said.\par     \par     WON\par     The won skidded 1.3 percent to 1,112.6 per dollar, its\par weakest since Dec. 9.\par     Offshore funds sold the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and South Korea's importers\par bought the dollar for payments.\par     The South Korean unit pared some of its losses as exporters\par chased it for settlements on dips, traders said.\par \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR\par     Change on the day at 0500 GMT\par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       120.96         120.84       -0.10\par   Sing dlr        1.3812         1.3775       -0.27\par   Taiwan dlr      31.523         31.450       -0.23\par   Korean won     1110.30        1098.70       -1.04\par   Baht             32.55          32.43       -0.38\par   Peso             44.27          44.09       -0.41\par   Rupiah        13060.00       12975.00       -0.65\par   Rupee            62.66          62.17       -0.78\par   Ringgit         3.6845         3.6530       -0.85\par   Yuan            6.2653    