\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Indonesia's c.bank says no target level for rupiah\b0\par\par\uc2 405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2015\par 06:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds chief economics minister)\par \par \uc2 JAKARTA, Feb 26 (Reuters) - \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have a target level for the rupiah but will always be in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for measured \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah fell to a 10-week low on Tuesday and is down nearly 4 percent so far this year, a trend which \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman \uc2 Peter Jacobs\uc2  attributed to the strengthening U.S. dollar and not due to \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's surprise decision last week to cut its benchmark interest rate.\par \par \uc2 "We cannot possibly go against the market," Jacobs said, adding that \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only to manage the rupiah's volatility.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut both its benchmark interest rate and its overnight deposit facility rate by 25 basis points last week to 7.50 percent and 5.50 percent, respectively.\par \par \uc2 The policy adjustment could weigh on the rupiah in the near term, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 After a meeting with the president and \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's governor on Tuesday, Chief Economics Minister Sofyan Djalil told reporters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  significantly to defend the weakening rupiah.\par \par \uc2 "Why would we use our \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves to defend a falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it was because of external factors?" Djalil said.\par \par \uc2 "Our focus is improving domestic conditions and \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  shares the same view."\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's Governor Agus Martowardojo said last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  retained its tight monetary policy despite cutting rates.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also remains on alert for changes in global financial conditions as the U.S. Federal Reserve prepares to normalize monetary policy, he added.\par \par \uc2 ING predicts further rate cuts, arguing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's focus has shifted to supporting economic growth from the current account.\par \par \uc2 "We forecast one 25 basis point (bp) cut in 2Q and two 25 bp cuts in 4Q, when we expect inflation to fall sharply due to the November 2014 fuel price hike entering the base of comparison," ING economists said in a note on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Southeast Asia's largest economy posted its weakest growth in five years in 2014 as the end of the commodities boom and high interest rates weighed on investment and domestic demand. (Reporting by Adriana Nina Kusuma, Fransiska Nangoy, and Jakarta bureau; Writing by Gayatri Suroyo; Editing by Kim Coghill) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-26T06:03:41.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150226eb2q005xy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
