tion \par                                               times \par                                               the Fixed Rate Day Count Fraction \par                                               divided by \par                                               the Applicable Rate \par  \par                                               (and rounding, if necessary, \par                                               the entire resulting figure \par                                               to the nearest two decimal places, \par                                               with USD 0.005 being rounded \par                                               upwards). \par  \par                                               The "Applicable Rate" means \par                                               the rate determined by the Calculation \par                                               Agent that is equal to the IDR/U.S. \par                                               Dollar weighted average spot \par                                               rate in the interbank market \par                                               based on traded IDR/USD spot \par                                               \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions \par                                               during a specified time period \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 25-02-15 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                               which are captured on a real \par                                               time basis, expressed as the \par                                               amount of IDR per one USD published \par                                               by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  at approximately \par                                               10:00 a.m., Jakarta time, on \par                                               the Rate Fixing Date as the \par              