                      Following Business Day Convention \par        (c) Fixed Rate Interest Payment Date(s): \par                                                                 Annually on each February 4, commencing on February 4, \par                                                                 2016 and ending on, and including, \par                                                                 the Maturity Date. \par        (d) Interest Period:                                     Each period from and including each Interest Payment \par                                                                 Date to but excluding the next following \par                                                                 Interest Payment Date, provided that the initial \par                                                                 Interest Period will commence on and include \par                                                                 the Interest Commencement Date, and the final Interest \par                                                                 Period will end on but exclude the \par                                                                 Maturity Date. \par                                                                 For the purposes of the calculation of the Interest \par                                                                 Amount payable for any Interest Period, \par                                                                 there shall be no adjustment pursuant to the Business \par                                                                 Day Convention specified above. \par        (e) Fixed Rate Day Count Fraction(s):                    Actual/Actual (ICMA) \par        (f) Calculation of Interest Amount:                      As soon as practicable and in accordance with the \par                                                                 procedure specified herein, the Calculation \par                                                                 Agent will determine the IDR Rate (as defined below) \par                                                                 and calculate the amount of interest \par                                                                 payable (the "Interest Amount") with respect to each \par                                                                 minimum Authorized Denomination for the \par                                                                 relevant Interest Period. \par                                                                 The Interest Amount with respect to any Interest \par                                                                 Period shall be a USD amount calculated as \par                                                                 of the relevant Rate Fixing Date (as defined below) as \par                                                                 follows: \par                                                                 7.00% times the minimum Authorized Denomination \par                                                                 times \par                                                                 the Fixed Rate Day Count Fraction \par                                                                 divided by \par                                                                 the IDR Rate \par                                                                 (and rounding, if necessary, the entire resulting \par                                                                 figure to the nearest two decimal places, \par                                                                 with USD 0.005 being rounded upwards). \par                                                                 The "IDR Rate" means the rate determined by the \par                                                                 Calculation Agent that is equal to the USD/IDR \par                                                                 weighted average spot rate in the interbank market, \par                                                                 based on traded USD/IDR spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                                                 transactions during a specified time period which are \par                                                                 captured on a real time basis, expressed \par                                                                 as the amount of IDR per one USD, for settlement in \par                                                                 two Fixing Business Days, as published \par                                                                 by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  as the "Jakarta Interbank Spot \par                                                                 Dollar Rate USD - IDR", which appears on \par                                                                 \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ), or as \par                                                                 published on Thomson Reuters Screen JISDOR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 25-02-15 0700GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                                                 Page (or any replacement page or replacement service \par                                                                 as may be implemented for the purposes \par                                                                 of displaying the USD/IDR weighted average spot rate), \par                                                                 or as otherwise made available by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \par                                                                 Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or its successor as administrator), at \par                                                                 approximately 10:00 a.m., Jakarta time, \par                                                                 on the Rate Fixing Date. Fallback Provisions apply as \par                                                                 set out below. \par                                                                 The "Rate Fixing Date" means the date that is five (5) \par                                                                 Fixing Business Days prior to the applicable \par                                                                 Fixed Rate Interest Payment Date or Maturity Date, as \par                                                                 the case may be. The Rate Fixing Date \par                                                                 shall be subject to adjustment as follows: if the \par                                                                 scheduled date of the Rate Fixing Date is \par                                                                 not a Relevant Business Day, then the Rate Fixing Date \par                                                                 will be the first preceding day that \par                                                                 is a Relevant Business Day. \par                                                                 "Fixing Business Day" means a day (other than a \par                                                                 Saturday or a Sunday) on which banks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                                                 exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets are open for business in Jakarta. \par                                                                 "Fallback Provisions": Should no USD/IDR weighted \par                                                                 average spot rate appear on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par                                                                 website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ) as the "Jakarta Interbank Spot \par                                                                 Dollar Rate USD - IDR", or on Thomson \par                                                                 Reuters Screen JISDOR Page (or on such replacement \par                                                                 page or service as described above), or \par                                                                 be otherwise made available by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or its \par                                                                 successor as administrator), on the \par                                                                 Rate Fixing Date, then the IDR Rate with respect to \par                                                                 the relevant Interest Period shall be \par                                                                 determined by the Calculation Agent by requesting \par                                                                 quotations for the mid USD/IDR spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                                                 exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate from five banks active in the USD/IDR \par                                                                 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets \par                                                                 as selected by the Calculation Agent (such banks, the \par                                                                 "Reference Banks") either (i) at or \par                                                                 about 10:00 a.m. Jakarta time on the first calendar \par                                                                 day (other than a Saturday or a Sunday) \par                                                                 following the Rate Fixing Date, if such day is a \par                                                                 Relevant Business Day or (ii) at or about \par                                                                 10:00 a.m. Jakarta time on the Rate Fixing Date, if \par                                                                 the first calendar day (other than a Saturday \par                                                                 or a Sunday) following the Rate Fixing Date is not a \par                                                                 Relevant Business Day. \par                                                                 If five or four quotations are provided by Reference \par                                                                 Banks as requested, the IDR Rate shall \par                                                                 be the arithmetic mean (rounded to the nearest whole \par                                                                 IDR, with IDR 0.5 being rounded upwards) \par                                                                 of the remaining three or two such quotations \par                                                                 (expressed as the number of IDR per one USD), \par                                                                 as the case may be, after disregarding the highest \par                                                                 quotation and the lowest quotation; provided, \par                                                                 that if two or more quotations are the highest \par                                                                 quotations, then only one of such quotations \par                                                                 shall be disregarded; and provided further, that if \par                                                                 two or more quotations are the lowest \par                                                                 quotations, then only one of such lowest quotations \par                                                                 shall be disregarded. \par                                                                 If only three or two quotations are provided as \par                                                                 requested, the IDR Rate shall be the arithmetic \par                                                                 mean (rounded to the nearest whole IDR, with IDR 0.5 \par                                                                 being rounded upwards) of such quotations \par                                                                 (expressed as the number of IDR per one USD). \par                                                                 If only one or no quotations are provided as \par                                                                 requested, or if the Calculation Agent determines \par                                                                 in its sole discretion that no suitable Reference \par                                                                 Banks active in the USD/IDR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or \par                                                                 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets will provide quotations, the \par                                                                 Calculation Agent shall be entitled \par                                                                 to calculate the IDR Rate acting in good faith in a \par                                                       