ts successor \par                                                                 as administrator), at approximately 10:00 a.m., \par                                                                 Jakarta time, on the Rate Fixing Date. Fallback \par                                                                 Provisions apply as set out below. \par                                                                 The "Rate Fixing Date" means the date that is five (5) \par                                                                 Fixing Business Days prior to the applicable \par                                                                 Fixed Rate Interest Payment Date or Maturity Date, as \par                                                                 the case may be. \par                                                                 "Fixing Business Day" means a day (other than a \par                                                                 Saturday or a Sunday) on which banks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                                                 exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets are open for business in Jakarta. \par                                                                 "Fallback Provisions": Should no USD/IDR weighted \par                                                                 average spot rate appear on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par                                                                 website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ) as the "Jakarta Interbank Spot \par                                                                 Dollar Rate USD - IDR", or on Thomson \par                                                                 Reuters Screen JISDOR Page (or on such replacement \par                                                                 page or service as described above), or \par                                                                 be otherwise made available by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or its \par                                                                 successor as administrator), on the \par                                                                 Rate Fixing Date, then the IDR Rate with respect to \par                                                                 the relevant Interest Period shall be \par                                                                 determined by the Calculation Agent by requesting \par                                                                 quotations for the mid USD/IDR spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                                                 exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate from five banks active in the USD/IDR \par                                                                 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets \par                                                                 as selected by the Calculation Agent (such banks, the \par                                                                 "Reference Banks") either (i) at or \par                                                                 about 10:00 a.m. Jakarta time on the first calendar \par                                                                 day (other than a Saturday or a Sunday) \par                                                                 following the Rate Fixing Date, if such day is a \par                                                                 Relevant Business Day or (ii) at or about \par                                                                 10:00 a.m. Jakarta time on the Rate Fixing Date, if \par                                                      