\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Tumble as Worries Over Greece, Ukraine Escalate\b0\par\par\uc2 By Anjani Trivedi   \par \uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2015\par 04:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Fears of a default in Greece and an escalating conflict in Ukraine spilled over into emerging markets as investors fled for safer assets, sending \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia and other developing countries tumbling.\par \par \uc2 Indonesia's rupiah sank as much as 1% while South Africa's rand hovered close to its weakest in over a decade and the Malaysian ringgit's slide gathered steam.\par \par \uc2 From a political gridlock in Europe over the restructuring of Greece's mountain of debt, to unsuccessful cease-fire talks aimed at ending the conflict in Ukraine and a renewed slide in oil prices overnight, pockets of risk for investors are growing with emerging market assets bearing the brunt.\par \par \uc2 "The markets are going to be sensitive for a prolonged period over time, " said Kenneth Akintewe, a portfolio manager at \uc2 Aberdeen Asset Management\uc2  in Singapore, which has $504.1 billion under management. "The strong dollar view is beginning to exert itself again, more strongly."\par \par \uc2 The U.S. economy is on its way to a recovery even as growth in other parts of the world slows and central banks are stepping in to competitively devalue their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Moreover, the U.S. Federal Reserve is expected to raise interest rates, luring yield-hungry investors away from record low rates in the developing world and less risky assets elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Bond markets are also tumbling, sending yields surging and pointing to investors also pulling out of these markets. Yields move inversely to prices.\par \par \uc2 For investors, the weakness in Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, which have performed relatively well to their emerging market peers so far this year, is a surprise. As countries in Latin America and emerging Europe have grappled with domestic economic and political challenges, Asia has been resilient with signs of proactive new governments and central banks, and lower \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility.\par \par \uc2 Local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds in Indonesia, Turkey, Thailand and the Philippines were top performers in 2014. Just weeks ago, yields on Indonesia's bonds fell to multiyear lows as foreign investors poured into local government bond auctions.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sudden plunge Thursday had traders and dealers saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  and had sold $50 million to $100 million.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman from \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  said, "\uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is always in the market and will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if necessary to prevent the rupiah from falling too sharply." He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline was exacerbated due to the dollar's strength and fears that Greece may pull out from the eurozone, expectations of a U.S. interest-rate increase and the Russia-Ukraine conflict.\par \par \uc2 He declined to confirm if \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  had sold dollars Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Emerging markets have grappled with volatile portfolio and capital flows, as global investor sentiment waxes and wanes. Analysts from \uc2 HSBC\uc2  say this could lead to more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness "that could spill over to other asset classes, possibly prompting less dovish or even hawkish monetary policy and eventually lower economic growth."\par \par \uc2 In Greece, the rescue deal expires at the end of the month and the government could run out of money in early March. With no agreement in sight with its creditors, analysts say Greece could exit the eurozone leading to widespread market turmoil, further dampening prospects of a European recovery. In Ukraine, world leaders are attempting to broker a cease-fire, and as of early Thursday there were only conflicting signs of progress.\par \par \uc2 -- to I-Made Sentana contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 13-02-15 0324GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020150213eb2d0003w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
