\par\par \b \uc2 Rupiah Gains After Fed Comments, \uc2 Bank  \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia \highlight \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,755 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Dezember 2014\par 06:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0501 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The USD/IDR slid to 12,570 vs. 12,630 late Wednesday as foreign investors bought high-yielding emerging assets after the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee said it can be patient in normalizing its monetary-policy stance. Bank Indonesia Senior Deputy Gov. \uc2 Mirza Adityaswara\uc2  said it sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, albeit a reduced amount vs. a day earlier. Dealers say the move is likely a sign the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stands ready to supply dollars. While \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Thursday, it could supply dollars later in the day if demand emerges from importers or companies paying down offshore debt. USD/IDR levels between 12,100-12,300 are "not a problem for (\uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 )," said Mr. Adityaswara, adding that a slightly undervalued rupiah would help to narrow the current-account deficit. (i-made.sentana@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: FLS \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0424 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The USD/INR pair is trading above its bullish gap and remains on the upside. The RSI is above its neutrality area at 50 and is reversing up. Even though a continuation of the consolidation cannot be ruled out, its extent should be limited. As long as the lower boundary of the gap at 62.96 is not broken, we favor long positions with targets at 64 and 64.5 in extension. A break below 62.96 would look for further downside with 62.5 and 62.2 as targets. In conclusion, we remain cautiously positive now, as long as 12625 is support. Below 12625, expect 12598 and 12582 in extension. For more information about TRADING Central please call by phone: London office (+44) 207 429 3980, Paris office (+33) 1 5528 8040 or email: sales@tradingcentral.com ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 ) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0422 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The strength in the U.S. dollar could have a downward impact on commodities over the next 6-12 months, but its impact could be offset by demand-supply fundamentals, Daniel Hynes, senior commodity strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 ANZ Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. "Fundamentals can't be ignored, and can disrupt the long-term negative correlation between the USD and commodities," he says. Hynes says each commodity will react differently to the rising greenback. Strong physical demand could blunt the impact of a stronger greenback on precious metals, while the correlation between the dollar and the oil price has moved into negative territory, in part due to OPEC's reluctance to cut output in an oversupplied market, he says. Nymex WTI crude is up 11 cents at $56.58/bbl, Brent crude is up 25 cents at $61.43/bbl. (eric.yep@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0420 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/IDR intraday: Cautiously positive. Technically, the USD/IDR is pulling back to test its horizontal level at 12625. The intraday RSI is mixed, calling for caution. Meanwhile, the MACD has just crossed below its signal line but is still positive. The configuration is mixed to bullish. Moreover, both its 20 and 50 MAs (respectively at 12589.244 and 12426.3926) now play support roles, which should prevent any downside potential. In conclusion, we remain cautiously positive now, as long as 12625 is support. Below 12625, expect 12598 and 12582 in extension. For more information about TRADING Central please call by phone: London office (+44) 207 429 3980, Paris office (+33) 1 5528 8040 or email: sales@tradingcentral.com (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0417 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/PHP continues to consolidate above its key support at 44.659. The RSI remains above its neutrality area at 50, and the MACD is also positive and above its signal line. Thus the configuration remains positive. Moreover, the pair is trading above both its 20 and 50 MAs (respectively at 44.6588 and 44.6509). Thus, as long as 44.659 holds as the key support, we maintain our bullish view with 44.843 and 44.888 as next targets. Alternatively, the downside breakout of 44.659 would call for further consolidations to 44.623 and 44.601. For more information about TRADING Central please call by phone: London office (+44) 207 429 3980, Paris office (+33) 1 5528 8040 or email: sales@tradingcentral.com (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0414 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] As long as 32.932 is support for USD/THB, look for 33.029. From a technical standpoint, the pair holds above its key intraday support at 32.932, and remains almost unchanged compared to last trading session. The intraday oscillator RSI is above 50. The MACD is positive and below its signal line. The pair could retrace to re-test the key level before a new rise. Moreover, the pair is trading under its 20 MA (32.9761) but above its 50 MA (32.8968). In this case, we expect a limited consolidation before a strong rebound to 33.029. Alternative scenario, only the downside breakout of 32.932 would open the path to 32.905 and 32.889. For more information about TRADING Central please call by phone: London office (+44) 207 429 3980, Paris office (+33) 1 5528 8040 or email: sales@tradingcentral.com (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0406 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Technically, USD/MYR remains in consolidation on an intraday basis. The failure of break above its nearest resistance around 3.50 should be a negative signal. Besides, the recent downside breakout of an intraday rising trend line has also confirmed an intraday bearish reversal. Regarding technical indicators, the RSI is trading below 30. This could mean that either the pair is in a lasting downtrend or just oversold and that therefore a rebound could shape (look for bullish divergence in this case). The MACD is positive and below its signal line. The MACD must penetrate its zero line to expect further downside. At last, the pair is trading under its 20 MA (3.4927) but above its 50 MA (3.4841). In conclusion, as long as 3.496 holds on the upside, look for further consolidations to 3.473 and 3.469. Alternatively, below 1.305 look for further downside with 1.3 and 1.296 as targets. For more information about TRADING Central please call by phone: London office (+44) 207 429 3980, Paris office (+33) 1 5528 8040 or email: sales@tradingcentral.com (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0403 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/SGD Intraday: further upside. From a chartist point of view, the pair posted a strong rebound in the previous trading session, and jumped above 1.31, representing a key horizontal level. The upward momentum has been resumed, as the intraday RSI indicator remains positively oriented (even within its "overbought" area above 70%), without displaying any reversal signals. Last but not least, the 20 & 50 MAs are turning up, confirming a bullish outlook. In these perspectives, suggest long positions above 1.305 with targets at 1.3175 and 1.324 in extension. Alternatively, below 1.305 look for further downside with 1.3 & 1.296 as targets. For more information about TRADING Central please call by phone: London office (+44) 207 429 3980, Paris office (+33) 1 5528 8040 or email: sales@tradingcentral.com (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0402 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China will likely ease fiscal and monetary policies next year to shield overall growth from a property market downturn, but the efforts may not be enough to prevent economic growth from slipping further, \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  economists say. "Ultimately however, they will be insufficient to halt and reverse China's structural property downturn and consequent softening of domestic demand," they say in a note to clients. The Chinese economy will likely grow 6.8% in 2015, slowing from the 7.3% anticipated for 2014 as property-related headwinds overwhelm any uplift from the U.S. recovery or intensified policy support, they add. Property new starts will likely decline by another 10-15% in 2015, weighing down more heavily on overall construction and the broader economy, they say. (liyan.qi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0400 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] While USD/KRW is posting a rebound from the recent low of 1080, it is still capped by the key resistance level at 1097. At the same time the 20-period moving average and the RSI are on the rise, caution is therefore advised. We suggest short positions below 1097 with targets at 1080 and 1070 in extension. Above 1097 look for further upside with 1106.2 and 1110.9 as targets. For more information about TRADING Central please call by phone: London office (+44) 207 429 3980, Paris office (+33) 1 5528 8040 or email: sales@tradingcentral.com (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0400 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Thailand's tourism sector may have finally turned a corner, but the pace of its recovery will be hampered by weaknesses in some key markets, says Capital Economics. Visitor arrivals grew by an average of 4.2% on-year in October and November, led by a 63% jump in Chinese tourists. The tourism sector--which accounts for roughly 10% of Thailand's gross domestic product--suffered from the political crisis throughout the first 9 months this year. The improvement should support the Thai economy going into 2015. However, weaknesses in Europe, a key tourism market, are a headwind. "With the European economies struggling, the performance of this sub-sector is likely to be lackluster," it says. Russian tourists, the fastest growing group, which accounted for a quarter of European visitors, will probably disappoint in light of the recent fall of the ruble. (warangkana.chomchuen@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @waanspeaking) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0357 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/TWD keeps trading within a bullish channel started in early December, while the RSI is pointing upwards calling for a new rise. Both the rising 20-period and 50-period moving averages are supporting USD/TWD. We suggest long positions above 31.17 with targets at 31.4 and 31.44 in extension. Below 31.17 look for further downside with 31.09 and 30.98 as targets. For more information about TRADING Central please call by phone: London office (+44) 207 429 3980, Paris office (+33) 1 5528 8040 or email: sales@tradingcentral.com (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.tradingcentral.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.tradingcentral.com}}}\uc2 \f2 ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 18, 2014 00:03 ET (05:03 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141218eaci000l8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
