\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  Steps Up Efforts to Defend Rupiah\b0\par\par\uc2 By I Made Sentana   \par \uc2 523 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2014\par 13:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA--Indonesia stepped up efforts on Tuesday to defend the rupiah as it continued to fall to levels unseen since the 1998 Asian financial crisis, underscoring the vulnerability of Southeast Asia's largest economy to fund outflows.\par \par \uc2 "We have been actively supplying [dollars] and buying government bonds," Senior Deputy Gov. \uc2 Mirza Adityaswara\uc2  said, adding that the rupiah has fallen below the 11,500-12,000 level that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deems good for both exports and imports.\par \par \uc2 Central bankers refused to disclose the amount of U.S. dollars sold Tuesday, but Deputy Gov. Perry Warjiyo confirmed it increased its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "We will continue to be in the market," Mr. Warjiyo told The Wall Street Journal.\par \par \uc2 Traders estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  likely sold around $500 million Tuesday. That would be about double the roughly $250 million it has sold daily on average since last week as global investors retreated from risky markets in expectation of a U.S. rate hike.\par \par \uc2 The rupiah fell to a new 16-year low of 12,900 to the dollar at one point early Tuesday from 12,700 late Monday, in line with the plunge in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of other countries whose finances likewise have been hurt by the decline in commodity prices.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2 's move seemed to help the rupiah--at least early on--as the dollar retreated to 12,690 in the late Asian session. But, economists said, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone may not be sufficient to shield the rupiah if a large portion of what economists estimate to be a $11.6 billion inflow to Indonesia so far this year reverses direction.\par \par \uc2 "Should the selloff continue due to deteriorating global risk sentiments, we wouldn't be surprised if this pushes the USD/IDR toward the 13,000-region and beyond in the near-term," Maybank said in a research note Tuesday, after \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has slid throughout this year, but the fall accelerated on Monday.\par \par \uc2 President Joko Widodo last month raised fuel prices by more than 30%, a bold measure that gave a short-lived confidence to the market that the government is committed to economic reform. But longer-term concerns emerged.\par \par \uc2 Tumbling global oil prices, which should be a net positive for Indonesia, continued to drag commodity prices lower. Along with the country's fiscal and monetary tightness, this will likely keep growth below 6% in 2015, economists said. The price of coal, one of Indonesia's main exports, has fallen heavily this year.\par \par \uc2 Yet Indonesia remains an attractive investment destination for brave portfolio investors, with interesting stock-picking opportunities if they know where to look, said Bharat Joshi, fund manager for \uc2 Aberdeen Asset Management\uc2  in Jakarta. "Despite the many challenges, there are companies that pass our strict quality control tests and are well positioned to take advantage of the growing domestic consumption," Mr. Joshi said.\par \par \uc2 Jake Maxwell Watts in Singapore contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to I Made Sentana at i-made.sentana@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 16, 2014 07:53 ET (12:53 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141216eacg001rg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\