\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED-Central banks  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  as Asia puts its strength to the test\b0\par\par\uc2 671 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2014\par 11:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects to say traders say RBI has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , RBI has not confirmed any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )               \par \par \uc2 * Asian central banks ramp up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid EM sell-off               \par \par \uc2 * Selldown rekindles painful memories of Asian financial crisis               \par \par \uc2 * Analysts say this not a repeat of 97/98 but warn of more losses               \par \par \uc2 By Nicholas Owen and Nachum Kaplan               \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA/SINGAPORE Dec 16 (Reuters) - Asian central banks have ramped up their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem the sell-off roiling emerging markets, testing the notion that the region is better placed to handle a market rout than during its 1997-1998 financial crisis.               \par \par \uc2 This battle between central banks and investors selling emerging market assets will likely intensify as analysts warn the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are set to slide further, pushed lower by falling commodity prices and the prospect of a U.S. rate hike.               \par \par \uc2 "Lower oil prices, weaker commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , lower material and oil service costs and increased efficiency are all reinforcing to the downside," wrote \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  in a report.               \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  confirmed it sold dollars on Tuesday, with traders saying the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  and \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\uc2  have been doing so as well in recent weeks.               \par \par \uc2 That comes as investors have dumped emerging market assets globally on tumbling oil prices and low growth prospects, with the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp hike in interest rates on Tuesday spooking markets further.               \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah hit its lowest level since 1998 for the second day running and the Indian rupee dropped to a 13 month low on Tuesday.               \par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to reduce volatility rather than defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the Indonesian finance minister also said it would buy back government bonds in the secondary market if necessary to stem capital outflows.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  has also sold dollars to ease the severity of the rupee's fall, according to traders.               \par \par \uc2 "It is still not an alarming situation but we have to see how far the rupee drifts from current levels," a \uc2 Indian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told Reuters, adding they would only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  "strongly" if there were large outflows.               \par \par \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\uc2  declined to confirm \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  when asked by Reuters, while \uc2 Bank of Thailand\uc2  bank said there "was no need to act" and no abnormal outflows despite Thai stocks slumping to their lowest levels since June 2.                              \par \par \uc2 MORE FALLS AHEAD               \par \par \uc2 Analysts think further falls in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are likely when the expected rise in U.S. interest rate materialises.               \par \par \uc2 "The weakness of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes at a time when the Fed hasn't even increased interest rates yet," said Khoon Goh, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ANZ bank in Singapore.               \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  holds its policy meeting this week, concluding Wednesday, and any signal that rates could rise soon could spark further emerging market selling.               \par \par \uc2 However despite the risks, analysts point to big differences between Asia now and in 1997/98.               \par \par \uc2 Most emerging Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  now float freely whereas they used to have pegged exchange rates.               \par \par \uc2 Central banks also have deeper foreign reserve and swap lines with other central banks that give them access to more dollars.               \par \par \uc2 "Part of the reason we saw a crisis in 1997 was that back then \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were overvalued and a lot of the countries were running large current-account deficits," said ANZ's Goh.               \par \par \uc2 "This time around the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are not overvalued."               \par \par \uc2 Only Indonesia and India are running current account deficits while external debt is lower too.               \par \par \uc2 Within Southeast Asia today, Thailand is the most exposed with foreign liabilities equal to 39 percent of GDP, still well below the 60 percent seen in 1996.               \par \par \uc2 However there are risks beyond headline numbers. Indonesia's external debt is a modest 34.7 percent of GDP yet its shallow capital markets mean that it borrows about 38 percent of its local debt from foreigners, according to the finance ministry, highlighting the risk from a sovereign perspective.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-16T11:50:06.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141216eacg009gl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
