\par\par \b \uc2 SE Asia Stocks -Down; extends losses on sell-off in emerging markets\b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2014\par 11:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par JAKARTA, Dec 16 (Reuters) - Southeast Asian stock markets\par extend losses on Tuesday after a fall in the Russian rouble\par triggered a sell-off in emerging markets due to global risk\par aversion.\par     The slump in the rouble on the back of falling oil prices\par and Western sanctions has sent emerging market investors into a\par panic, analysts said, prompting U.S. dollar buying which hurt\par local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and stock prices in Southeast Asia. \par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sharply hiked interest rates early on\par Tuesday to support the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but after a brief recovery the\par rouble fell to a new all-time low against the dollar.\par  \par     Thai stocks fell as much as 3.9 percent led by\par energy stocks before recovering some losses to close 1.1 percent\par down for the day, a sixth consecutive day of falls.\par     Shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 PTT Exploration and Production PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell\par 5.2 percent to their lowest since April 2009, while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bangchak\par Petroleum PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  lost 4.1 percent to its lowest in more\par than four months.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it did not see "unusual capital\par outflow" from the country despite foreign investors posting\par about 14 billion baht ($424.89 million) of net sales in the past\par four sessions to Monday. \par     Indonesian stocks fell 1.6 percent, extending a 1\par percent decline from the previous session, after the rupiah\par  hit a fresh 16-year low early on Tuesday. Later, the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recovered after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par and bond markets. \par     Singapore's stock index lost 2.4 percent while the\par Philippines fell 1.6 percent.\par \par     \par For Asian Companies click;  \par For South East Asia Hot Stock reports, click;\par    \par \par SOUTHEAST ASIAN STOCK MARKETS\par  Change on day\par  Market             Current     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Singapore          3215.09       3294.14       -2.40\par  Kuala Lumpur       1673.94       1697.31       -1.38\par  Bangkok            1461.74       1478.49       -1.13\par  Jakarta            5026.03       5108.43       -1.61\par  Manila             7160.38       7275.62       -1.58\par  Ho Chi Minh         535.14        547.93       -2.33\par  \par  Change on year\par  Market             Current       End 2013    Pct Move\par  Singapore          3215.09       3167.43       +1.50\par  Kuala Lumpur       1673.94       1866.96       -10.4\par  Bangkok            1461.74       1298.71       +12.6\par  Jakarta            5026.03       4274.18       +17.6\par  Manila             7160.38       5889.83       +21.6\par  Ho Chi Minh         535.14        504.63       +6.04\par  ($1 = 32.9500 baht)\par \par  (Reporting by Fransiska Nangoy; Editing by Sunil Nair)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-16T11:07:48.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141216eacg009fs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
