\par\par \b \uc2 Bank Indo Confirms  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  as Rupiah Drops to 1998 Lows -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,584 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2014\par 08:53\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0753 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirms it has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rupiah and bond prices after the rupiah dropped to levels unseen since the 1998 Asian financial crisis. Senior deputy governor \uc2 Mirza Adityaswara\uc2  says it will continue to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He says rupiah's ideal range is 11,500-12,000 to the dollar, which he says is good both for exports and imports. However, the rupiah fell to as low as 12,900 to the dollar in the morning, requiring \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has brought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back to around 12,700. He says the rupiah weakness will likely be temporary and due to external factors such as expectations of a U.S. rate hike and investor jitters towards emerging markets.\par \par \uc2  Domestically, Indonesia's current-account deficit is also contributing to the negative sentiment toward the rupiah, but he says that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government have taken efforts to narrow the deficit, which he expects will drop to $25 billion this year from $29 billion last year. (i-made.sentana@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0750 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Both the French services and manufacturing PMIs (0800 GMT) are expected to move further into contraction at 47.5 and 48.0 respectively from 47.9 and 48.4 Seen in November according to the analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Germany (0830 GMT) however, is expected to see manufacturing edge back into expansion at 50.0 vs 49.5 last, while services also improves to 52.5 vs 52.1. The bank sees a mixed run for the Eurozone (0900 GMT) prints, with manufacturing unchanged at 50.1, while services slips to 50.8 from 51.1 seen in November. EUR/USD now at 1.2456. gary.stride@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0749 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China government bonds are higher Tuesday after the country posted weak initial PMI data for December. The benchmark seven-year government bond yield is down at 3.73% vs 3.77% Monday. "Some investors are speculating that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  may roll out more easing measures like reserve requirement ratio cut to boost the growth and to inject liquidity to meet rising demand at year-end," says a Shanghai-based local bank trader. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 PBOC\f28 \uc2 \f2  again didn't act in Tuesday's open-market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , raising hopes that it may resort to other measure to add liquidity into the system. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0749 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Lower oil prices will have a significant impact on government budgets in the Persian Gulf but the region is in better shape than other global oil-exporters because it has sufficient fiscal reserves, says an \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2  official. "There is a significant impact here (GCC) on fiscal revenues," says Harald Finger of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2 . However, reckons the GCC countries have sufficient reserves through sovereign wealth funds and in foreign assets to withstand the impact of low oil prices and therefore there is no need in a quick reduction in spending. Says low oil price environment offers opportunity to review energy subsidies in the region. (nicolas.parasie@wsj.com; Twitter: @NicolasParasie) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0743 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Away from its U.K.-focused stress tests, the BOE's main financial stability worries once again arise from the eurozone, with the twice-yearly Financial Stability Report warning that a loss of confidence in the ability of the ECB and others to boost growth and inflation could lead to a revival of market tensions last seen in 2011 and 2012, with bank funding costs on the rise. However, the FSR points out that banks are generally better capitalized across Europe than they were back then, while UK banks have cut their eurozone exposures, and eurozone banks have cut their UK lending. Of course, it could all turn nasty were "any euro-area member country to lose access to market funding." Like Greece, for example. (paul.hannon@wsj.com. Twitter: @PaulHannon29) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0740 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The governor of the Bank of Thailand says baht weakening is in line with regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the "medium-level" fluctuation is nothing to worry about. The Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has depreciated to almost 33 baht per dollar, but the volume of capital outflow is still normal, which means \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  measures aren't necessary, says Prasarn Trairatvorakul, the Thai central banker. The drop of Stock Exchange of Thailand on Monday could be attributed to the decline of global oil prices, which prompted investors to sell shares in oil and petrochemical companies, Prasarn says. (warangkana.chomchuen@wsj.com; Twitter: @waanspeaking) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0735 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Markets traded with a definite risk-off tone overnight, the mood turning sour as stocks took a downturn Monday with the main European bourses shedding close to 3% and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 S&P\f28 \uc2 \f2  ending 0.6% lower. That gave Asia an excuse to book profit on USD longs, with USD/JPY sinking to a fresh 1-month low as the Nikkei closed down 2% and China's flash PMI falling into contraction at a 7-month low 49.5 didn't help sentiment any either. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Russian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hiked rates by 650 bps to 17% to try and stem the ruble's collapse, but so far it has had limited success with USD/RUB currently trading at 62.00, from Monday's fresh all-time high of 66.42. The RBA's December meeting held little new information with the usual mantra of AUD being too strong still included, AUD/USD currently trades at 4-year lows. Up ahead it's a crowded data slate with European flash PMIs, German ZEW, UK inflation and the Riksbank rate decision. gary.stride@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0733 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes the month of November saw a 2% drop in UK petrol pump prices, heavy discounting around Black Friday and Cyber Monday, a drop in global food and commodity prices and ongoing intense competition between supermarkets that is likely to have kept food inflation low. It's little wonder that the bank is forecasting CPI at zero on the month and +1.2% on the year against +0.1% and +1.3% seen in October, while RPI drops by 0.1% to 2.2% on the year. GBP/USD now at 1.5660. gary.stride@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0733 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Parts of the Pacific Ocean are close to or have breached the threshold temperatures for an El Nino event, says the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Australian Bureau of Meteorology\f28 \uc2 \f2  Tuesday. The weather event is not considered to be underway however, as some atmospheric indicators have not shown sustained and widespread patterns consistent with the phenomenon, it adds. The bureau says there is now a greater-than-70% chance that the event will occur. El Nino is an abnormal warming of the Pacific Ocean that causes drought in some areas and flooding in others. It is usually associated with drier weather in Asia and, therefore, lower crop yields. The bureau said in early December that there was at least a 70% chance of an El Nino weather event in the coming months. (huileng.tan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0729 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]-- The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2 's stress testing gives most major UK banks a clean bill of health, although the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Co-Op Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  was asked to raise more capital. RBS and Lloyds were deemed to have passed, just, and don't need to raise any more at this point. The BoE said one of the things it tested for was resilience in the face of an imagined 35% fall in house prices. The overall finding was of more strength in the system overall now than in 2013. david.cottle@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0717 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Mumbai broker Prabhudas Lilladher says its channel checks suggest continued slackness in secondary sales or real demand for cement during December despite a weak base in October and November. November saw most cement makers reporting a strong growth. "But, this growth was not ... commensurate with growth in real sales," says Prabhudas Lilladher. This could possibly have been a "mere transfer" from cement makers' factories to dealers' warehouses, the broker says. Given the elevated inventory levels and the onset of the calendar year-end discounts, prices are expected to remain weak in December, says Prabhudas Lilladher. (kenan.machado@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0712 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--While the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's tightening should clearly have a positive effect on the ruble, in addition to the rate hike the regulator should at least reduce to a minimum - if not curtail - new volumes of ruble liquidity provided through refinancing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sberbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. It calls for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to initiate active \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , even at the cost of significantly depleting reserves. Alex.Kolyandr@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 16, 2014 02:53 ET (07:53 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141216eacg000xt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
