\par\par \b \uc2 EM ASIA  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rupiah hits 16-year low as Indonesian bonds retreat\b0\par\par\uc2 712 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2014\par 09:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Rupiah slides 1.6 percent, hits lowest since August 1998\par     * Year-end dollar demand, worsening risk sentiment dents\par rupiah\par     * Focus also on possible rupiah selling by offshore\par investors\par \par  (Adds comments, updates levels)\par     By Masayuki Kitano\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 15 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah hit a\par 16-year low versus the dollar on Monday, dented by year-end\par corporate demand for dollars and possible position squaring in\par Indonesian bonds by overseas investors.\par     The rupiah, like other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , has faltered in\par recent weeks as investors positioned for the U.S. Federal\par Reserve to start raising interest rates next year on the back of\par a gradual economic recovery in the United States.\par     Its fall accelerated over the past two trading sessions,\par with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hitting a low of 12,695 versus the dollar\par   on Monday, its lowest level since August 1998,\par according to Reuters data.\par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on Monday it is \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par both the bond and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to stabilise prices.\par   \par     The rupiah's weakness stood out on a mixed day overall for\par emerging Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , with the South Korean won \par and Singapore dollar, edging higher while \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par such as the Indian rupee retreated.\par     Market participants said the rupiah was hit by worsening\par global risk sentiment as well as year-end corporate demand for\par the greenback. \par     "Ahead of the end of year, we are seeing some increased\par onshore corporate demand for U.S. dollar, which is keeping\par dollar/IDR quite bid," said Divya Devesh, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist for\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Standard Chartered Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  in Singapore.\par     There was also focus on possible rupiah-selling linked to\par overseas investor holdings of Indonesian bonds.\par     "We have seen massive inflows into Indonesian bonds this\par year, and there seems to be a minor selloff in bonds as well, so\par people might be taking profit ahead of the year-end," said\par Devesh.\par     Indonesia's 10-year government bonds came under pressure on\par Monday, with their yields rising 11.6 basis points to 8.203\par percent, on track for the biggest one-day rise in\par yields since late September.\par     The rupiah's weakness in non-deliverable forwards (NDFs)\par since around Friday suggests that overseas investors are behind\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's latest drop, said Satoshi Okagawa, senior global\par markets analyst for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2  in\par Singapore.\par     "There are some visible signs of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hedging against\par rupiah weakness...by overseas investors," Okagawa said.\par     The rupiah fell as low as 12,908 versus the dollar on\par one-month NDFs, its lowest level since November\par 2008, according to Reuters data.\par \par     PHILIPPINE PESO\par     The peso edged lower versus the dollar but the\par drop was limited, thanks to some support in the wake of its\par sovereign rating upgrade last week.\par     Last week, the peso had touched a 2-1/2 month high versus\par the dollar at 44.470. That rise came after Moody's Investors\par Service upgraded its rating on the Philippines by one notch to\par Baa2 on Thursday, citing a decline in its debt burden and\par structural improvements in fiscal management. \par     \par     \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR \par                                           \par   Change on the day at   0733 GMT         \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       118.32         118.83       +0.43\par   Sing dlr        1.3114         1.3140       +0.20\par   Taiwan dlr      31.321         31.326       +0.02\par   Korean won     1098.42        1103.10       +0.43\par   Baht             32.78          32.78       +0.02\par   Peso             44.66          44.58       -0.18\par   Rupiah        12660.00       12455.00       -1.62\par   Rupee            62.70          62.28       -0.67\par   Ringgit         3.4950         3.4950       +0.00\par   Yuan            6.1876         6.1869       -0.01\par                                           \par   Change so far in 2014                   \par   \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par   Japan yen       118.32         105.28      -11.03\par   Sing dlr        1.3114         1.2632       -3.68\par   Taiwan dlr      31.321         29.950       -4.38\par   Korean won     1098.42        1055.40       -3.92\par   Baht             32.78          32.86       +0.26\par   Peso             44.66          44.40       -0.59\par   Rupiah        12660.00       12160.00       -3.95\par   Rupee            62.70          61.80       -1.44\par   Ringgit         3.4950         3.2755       -6.28\par   Yuan            6.1876         6.0539       -2.16\par           