\par\par \b \uc2 Indonesian Rupiah Bonds Fall; Rupiah at 16-Year Low -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2014\par 10:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0927 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Indonesian government rupiah bonds fall sharply Monday as foreign investors trim their holdings in risky assets from emerging markets such as Indonesia on expectations of rate hikes in the US, dealers say. "Yields rise by an average 25-basis points today; it's quite a significant one-day rise," says \uc2 Mandiri Sekuritas\uc2 's debt market analyst Handy Yunianto. The yields of the benchmark 10-year bond is up to 8.44% from 8.22 Friday. The selloff in bonds helps push the rupiah to its lowest level in 16 years, touching 12,695 against the U.S. dollar. Dealers say \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling around $100 million in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and buying government rupiah bonds. (i-made.sentana@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0922 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Taiwanese banks call for a wider scope of CNY business on the island, hoping to boost their razor-thin net interest margins. At an annual cross-Strait business forum in Taipei, Ho Show-chung, chairman of SinoPac, says Taiwanese banks' net interest margin averaged 1.4% as at the end of the third quarter, much lower than Chinese banks' 3.0%. Ho and Hua Nan Financial's chairman Liu Teng-cheng suggest scrapping the CNY20,000 daily limit of conversion in Taiwan--a limit that was lifted in Hong Kong recently. Liu also proposes to explore the possibility of a Taiwan-Shanghai stock market connect, mirroring the HK-Shanghai connect, and increasing quota for Taiwanese investment in Chinese local bond market.(aries.poon@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0918 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Investment Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the country's biggest sovereign fund, says it wants to explore investment targets in Taiwan, and may team up with Taiwanese investors on overseas projects. Speaking at an annual cross-Strait business forum in Taipei, CIC Chairman Ding Xuedong says Taiwan's strengths are in technology, agriculture and manufacturing sectors. "We are not looking for operating or management rights of target companies and sectors," says Ding. "We are willing to be minority financial investors...We are seeking returns on China's massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves." He adds CIC oversees US$700 billion assets, of which US$210 billion are outside of China. The fund doesn't have investments in Taiwan. (aries.poon@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0914 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Malaysia's insurance and 'takaful' sector--a co-operative system that acts like insurance--is expected to remain stable in 2015 as new regulations and market liberalization emerge, says a ratings agency. "The demand for investment-linked products will continue to drive growth in the life sector as consumers' risk appetites increase amid low interest rates. Higher private consumption will also sustain the growth in the general insurance sector's personal line products," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  said today. It also said the industry's risk-based capital remained strong at 250% in 1H2014. Fitch warned the sector outlook could be revised to negative if insurers are severely affected by operating losses from extreme equity market volatility or market-wide solvency issues. "It could also be revised if there is significant deterioration in underwriting losses from the compulsory motor class." (celine.fernandez@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0905 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  took a snapshot of its EUR/USD order book earlier today when the rate traded at 1.2456, and there were more sell orders than buys. It stays that way until levels around 1.2380, where the sell and buy densities are about equal. This, says the bank suggests that EUR/USD is currently under selling pressure, but that a downmove would run out of steam around the 1.2380 level. EUR/USD now at 1.2442. gary.stride@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0903 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Most Thai entrepreneurs are not expecting their businesses to fare much better in 2015 than in 2014, according to the latest survey by the Employers' Confederation of Thai Trade and Industry. Over 50% of operators in the industrial sector and the hotel and travel industries across Thailand surveyed by ECONTHAI say the situation next year will be more or less the same as this year. However, they expect overall economic conditions to improve markedly on stronger state spending and investment, which is estimated at 363 billion baht or $11.06 billion. ECONTHAI reports that 34.5% of surveyed entrepreneurs found their sales and earnings in 2014 contracted from a year ago while 34.9% said they were stable and 30.6% said business was better. (nopparat.chaichalearmmongkol@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0851 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Vietnam recorded a trade surplus of $437 million in November, compared with a deficit of $5 million in October, the Vietnam Customs Department says. Late last month, the government's statistics office estimated a trade deficit of $300 million for the month. Exports in November fell 6.0% on month at $13.23 billion, while imports were 9.1% lower at $12.79 billion, the department says. For the first 11 months of this year, exports rose 13.7% on year to $136.94 billion, while imports were up 11.8% at $134.06 billion, it adds. Vietnam's largest export earners in the Jan-Nov period were smart phones and electronics, garments, footwear, seafood and crude oil. Its key imports were machinery, electronics components, garment materials and fuels. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; Twitter @TrongKhanhVu) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0841 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Ride-sharing app Uber has another controversy on its hands. The company received a torrent of criticism online Monday after it automatically raised prices for riders in Sydney amid an unfolding siege at a caf\u233\'00\'E9. That was the result of an Uber algorithm underpinning its "surge pricing" model, which charges customers more during times of high demand. Some users reported the minimum fare had skyrocketed to $100 Australian dollars ($82) for a ride. Uber quickly backtracked, saying trips out of the downtown area would be free for riders. Meanwhile, governments around the world continue to question the company's legality, saying it competes unfairly with taxi firms, while earlier this month allegations that an Uber driver raped a woman in India triggered a nationwide ban on smartphone-enabled taxi services. (newley.purnell@wsj.com; Twitter: @Newley) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0834 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/TWD is slightly higher on thin volume, lifted by continued foreign fund outflows, say two local traders. The pair closes at 31.342--the highest onshore closing level over 50 months, versus 31.326 late Friday. They say the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is believed to have bought the USD around 31.320 (versus 31.300 Friday) to keep the pair in its target band. "Most market participants believe the New Taiwan dollar has room to depreciate more as its recent declines still lag behind other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," a trader says. But buying in USD weakened after the USD/TWD rose above 31.330 as some investors turned cautious following rebounds in the JPY and the KRW and ahead of the FOMC meeting, the trader adds. Foreign investors have been net sellers of local stocks for seven straight sessions. (fanny.liu@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0818 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--SEB notes that today the Swedish Premium Pension Authority pays out annual capital to various mutual funds chosen by Sweden's six million pension savers. Historically, a large share of the funds are invested in foreign assets which results in negative SEK flows. The general pattern is that EUR/SEK tends to rise ahead of PPM day, and keep on climbing for 5 days, turning down on the sixth day until around 21 days after PPM day. The bank says if the cross follows this pattern, then it will head higher until around December 22, and then fall around January 12. EUR/SEK traded at a 4-year high of 9.4180 both Friday and today, now at 9.4030. gary.stride@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0807 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China government bonds are down as liquidity tightens with a slew of IPOs hitting the market, increasing demand for cash ahead of the New Year holiday. The seven-year government bond yield is up at 3.77% vs 3.74%. But investors aren't too worried about the bonds, saying some bonds are starting to look appealing after their recent falls. On Thursday, 12 IPOs will start to open subscriptions, expecting to raise around $2.2 billion in total. (wynne.wang@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0749 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Indonesian rupiah plummeted to its weakest level since 1998 during the Asian Financial Crisis, on Monday, as global investors retreat from risky markets and a commodity slide hurts the country's finances. The Indonesia rupiah touched 12,695 against the U.S. dollar Monday and last traded at 12,660. On Friday, the rupiah closed at 12,455. As the year draws to a close, money managers are looking ahead to 2015 and cutting down on risky or vulnerable positions in emerging markets like Indonesia. Many are also bracing for turmoil in emerging markets as the U.S. dollar strengthens and growth in the U.S. beats much of the rest of the world. The rupiah started the year well, climbing 7.5% until early April, with investors pinning their hopes on the election of pro-reform President Joko Widodo, who would support a good mix of monetary policy and economic reform. But since he took office in late July, the rupiah has fallen close to 9%. (anjani.trivedi@wsj.com; Twitter @anjani_trivedi) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 15, 2014 04:27 ET (09:27 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141215eacf000vj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
