\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Indonesia c.bank supports  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2 , bonds as rupiah at lowest since 1998\b0\par\par\uc2 621 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2014\par 09:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2014 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Rupiah falls 1.7 percent on the day               \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 Indonesia\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bond market               \par \par \uc2 * Increased dollar demand seen for year-end payments   (Recasts, adds details and comments)               \par \par \uc2 By Fransiska Nangoy and Masayuki Kitano               \par \par \uc2 JAKARTA/SINGAPORE, Dec 15 (Reuters) - The Indonesian rupiah tumbled to its lowest level since August 1998 on Monday as declining risk appetites and increasing demand for dollars to settle year-end foreign loan payments put pressure on the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , bonds and shares.               \par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  said that it was acting in both the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bond markets to help stabilise prices, as emerging markets from Europe to Latin America suffer sharp outflows of capital.               \par \par \uc2 The rupiah fell to 12,695 rupiah before paring its losses to 12,665 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was down 1.7 percent on the day - its biggest one-day drop in more than four months - and 4.3 percent this year.               \par \par \uc2 Analysts attributed the fall to a combination of factors including how the sharp drop in oil prices has increased pessimism about global growth, and a steady rise in the dollar on expectations the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will begin raising interest rates next year.               \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. continues to post positive economic data which in turn hit the rupiah," said Royke Tumilaar, head of treasury at \uc2 Bank Mandiri\uc2 .                              \par \par \uc2 'REALLY EXPOSED'               \par \par \uc2 "High foreign ownership in our capital markets makes us really exposed to a strengthening dollar," he added.               \par \par \uc2 The yield of the 10-year government bond rose to 8.203 percent from 8.087 percent on Friday. Traders said they believed state banks were buying bonds amid heavy foreign selling.               \par \par \uc2 At 0740 GMT,  the benchmark index for Indonesian shares was down 1.2 percent.               \par \par \uc2 Moves in rupiah's non-deliverable forwards suggest selling by overseas investors is behind the rupiah's latest drop, said Satoshi Okagawa, senior global markets analyst for \uc2 Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corporation\uc2  in Singapore.               \par \par \uc2 "There are some visible signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedging against rupiah weakness," Okagawa said.               \par \par \uc2 Divya Devesh, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for \uc2 Standard Chartered Bank\uc2  in Singapore, said that on top of weak risk appetites, year-end corporate demand for dollars plus profit-taking in Indonesian bonds may be weighing on the rupiah.                              \par \par \uc2 CHANGING FLOWS               \par \par \uc2 "We have seen massive inflows into Indonesian bonds this year, and there seems to be a minor selloff in bonds, so people might be taking profit ahead of the year-end," Devesh said.               \par \par \uc2 Wellian Wiranto, economist at Singapore's \uc2 OCBC Bank\uc2 , said  the rupiah "has been hit because of the relatively high degree of foreign ownership in its government bonds, which is not a plus point given the anticipation of broad strength in the US economy and dollar."               \par \par \uc2 Data from \uc2 Indonesia's Finance Ministry\uc2  shows an outflow of 11 trillion rupiah ($869.22 million) between Dec. 1 and Dec. 11, during which foreign ownership of total tradable bonds fell to 38.6 percent from a record high 39.5 percent.               \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's credit default swaps contacts were major underperformers on Monday. The 5-year contract  or the cost of insuring sovereign debt for 5 years rose 12 basis points (bps) to 167/177 basis points (bps) compared with the broad market index which widened by 6 bps.               \par \par \uc2 The rupiah's fall comes shortly after \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  (BI) showed increasing concern about the level of foreign borrowing by Indonesian companies.               \par \par \uc2 In October, BI issued a regulation - to take effect on Jan. 1 - that private firms should hedge 20 percent of their dollar needs to repay offshore loans six months prior to maturity. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has warned firms against unhedged loans.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-12-15T09:17:32.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020141215eacf005hp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
