\par\par \b \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\uc2  Issue of Debt\b0\par\par\uc2 3,636 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 2014\par 18:06\par \uc2 Regulatory News Service\par \uc2 RNS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014   \par \par \uc2 TIDM94HD\par \par \uc2 RNS Number : 5456U\par \par \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\par \par \uc2 16 October 2014\par \par \uc2 PRICING SUPPLEMENT\par \par \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\par \par \uc2 Global Debt Program\par \par \uc2 Series No: 482\par \par \uc2 Tranche No: 2\par \par \uc2 IDR 250,000,000,000 7.35 percent Notes due September 12, 2018 (the "Notes") as from October 16, 2014 to be consolidated and form a single series with the Bank's IDR 1,000,000,000,000 7.35 percent Notes due September 12, 2018, issued on September 12, 2014 (the "Series 482 Tranche 1 Notes")\par \par \uc2 payable in United States Dollars\par \par \uc2 Issue Price: 99.37 percent plus 34 days' accrued interest\par \par \uc2 Application has been made for the Notes to be admitted to the Official List of the \uc2 United Kingdom Listing Authority\uc2  and to trading on the \uc2 London Stock Exchange plc\uc2 's Regulated Market\par \par \uc2 Citigroup Global Markets Limited\par \par \uc2 The date of this Pricing Supplement is as of October 9, 2014\par \par \uc2 Terms used herein shall be deemed to be defined as such for the purposes of the Terms and Conditions (the "Conditions") set forth in the Prospectus dated January 8, 2001 (the "Prospectus") (which for the avoidance of doubt does not constitute a prospectus for the purposes of Part VI of the United Kingdom Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 or a base prospectus for the purposes of Directive 2003/71/EC of the \uc2 European Parliament\uc2  and of the Council). This Pricing Supplement must be read in conjunction with the Prospectus. This document is issued to give details of an issue by the \uc2 Inter-American Development Bank\uc2  (the "Bank") under its Global Debt Program and to provide information supplemental to the Prospectus. Complete information in respect of the Bank and this offer of the Notes is only available on the basis of the combination of this Pricing Supplement and the Prospectus.\par \par \uc2 Terms and Conditions\par \par \uc2 The following items under this heading "Terms and Conditions" are the particular terms which relate to the issue the subject of this Pricing Supplement. These are the only terms which form part of the form of Notes for such issue.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  1.     Series No.:                        482 \par          Tranche No.:                       2 \par  2.     Aggregate Principal Amount:        IDR 250,000,000,000 \par                                             As from the Issue Date, the Notes \par                                             will be consolidated and form \par                                             a single series with the Series \par                                             482 Tranche 1 Notes. \par  3.     Issue Price:                       IDR 250,160,416,666.67, which \par                                             amount represents the sum of (a) \par                                             99.37 percent of the Aggregate \par                                             Principal Amount plus (b) the \par                                             amount of IDR 1,735,416,666.67 \par                                             representing 34 days' accrued \par                                             interest, inclusive. \par  \par                                             The Issue Price will be payable \par                                             in USD in the amount of USD 20,575,786.86 \par                                             at the agreed rate of 12,158 IDR \par                                             per one USD. \par  4.     Issue Date:                        October 16, 2014 \par         Form of Notes \par          (Condition 1(a)):                  Registered only, as further provided \par                                             in paragraph 9(c) of "Other Relevant \par    5.                                       Terms" below. \par  6.     Authorized Denomination(s) \par           (Condition 1(b)):                 IDR 10,000,000 and integral multiples \par                                             thereof \par  7.     Specified \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par          (Condition 1(d)):                  The lawful \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of the Republic \par                                             of Indonesia ("Indonesian Rupiah" \par                                             or "IDR"), provided that all payments \par                                             in respect of the Notes will be \par                                             made in United States Dollars \par                                             ("U.S.$" or "USD") \par  8.     Specified Principal Payment \par          \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par          (Conditions 1(d) and 7(h)):        USD \par  9.     Specified Interest Payment \par          \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            USD \par          (Conditions 1(d) and 7(h)): \par  10.    Maturity Date \par          (Condition 6(a); Fixed              September 12, 2018 \par          Interest Rate): \par  11.    Interest Basis \par          (Condition 5):                     Fixed Interest Rate (Condition \par                                             5(I)) \par  12.    Interest Commencement Date \par          (Condition 5(III)):                 September 12, 2014 \par  13.    Fixed Interest Rate (Condition     Condition 5(I) as amended and \par          5(I)):                             supplemented below, shall apply \par                                             to the Notes. The bases of the \par                                             Calculation of the Interest Amount, \par                                             Interest Payment Dates and default \par                                             interest are as set out below. \par  \par           (a) Interest Rate:                7.35 percent per annum \par         (b) Business Day Convention:       Following Business Day Convention \par         (c) Fixed Rate Interest \par          Payment Date(s):                    Annually on each September 12, \par                                              commencing on September 12, 2015 \par                                              and ending on, and including, \par                                              the Maturity Date. \par         (d) Interest Period:               Each period from and including \par                                             each Interest Payment Date to \par                                             but excluding the next following \par                                             Interest Payment Date, provided \par                                             that the initial Interest Period \par                                             will commence on and include the \par                                             Interest Commencement Date, and \par                                             the final Interest Period will \par                                             end on but exclude the Maturity \par                                             Date. \par                                             For the purposes of the calculation \par                                             of the Interest Amount payable \par                                             for any Interest Period, there \par                                             shall be no adjustment pursuant \par                                             to the Business Day Convention \par                                             specified above. \par         (e) Fixed Rate Day Count \par          Fraction(s):                       30/360 \par         (f) Calculation of Interest        As soon as practicable and in \par          Amount:                            accordance with the procedure \par                                             specified herein, the Calculation \par                                             Agent will determine the Applicable \par                                             Rate (as defined below) and calculate \par                                             the amount of interest payable \par                                             (the "Interest Amount") with respect \par                                             to each minimum Authorized Denomination \par                                             for the relevant Interest Period. \par                                             The Interest Amount with respect \par                                             to any Interest Period shall be \par                                             a USD amount calculated on the \par                                             relevant Fixing Date (as defined \par                                             below) as follows: \par                                             7.35% times minimum Authorized \par                                             Denomination \par                                             times \par                                             the Fixed Rate Day Count Fraction \par                                             divided by \par                                             the Applicable Rate \par  \par                                             (and rounding, if necessary, the \par                                             entire resulting figure to the \par                                             nearest two decimal places, with \par                                             USD 0.005 being rounded upwards). \par  \par                                             The "Applicable Rate" means the \par                                             rate determined by the Calculation \par                                             Agent that is equal to the IDR/U.S. \par                                             Dollar weighted average spot rate \par                                             in the interbank market based \par                                             on traded IDR/USD spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                             exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  transactions during a \par                                             specified time period which are \par                                             captured on a real time basis, \par                                             expressed as the amount of IDR \par                                             per one USD published by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank \par                                             Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  at approximately 10:00 \par                                             a.m., Jakarta time, on the Rate \par                                             Fixing Date as the "Jakarta Interbank \par                                             Spot Dollar Rate USD - IDR", which \par                                             appears on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 16-10-14 1606GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                             (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ), Thomson Reuters \par                                             Screen JISDOR Page, Bloomberg \par                                             Page JISDOR, or otherwise made \par                                             available by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or \par                                             its successor as administrator). \par                                             Fallback Provisions apply as per \par                                             below. \par                                            The "Fixing Date" means the date \par                                             that is five (5) IDR Business \par                                             Days prior to the applicable Interest \par                                             Payment Date or Maturity Date, \par                                             as the case may be. The Fixing \par                                             Date shall be subject to adjustment \par                                             as follows: if the scheduled date \par                                             of the Fixing Date is not a Relevant \par                                             Business Day, then the Fixing \par                                             Date will be the first preceding \par                                             day that is a Relevant Business \par                                             Day. \par                                             "IDR Business Day" means a day \par                                             (other than a Saturday or a Sunday) \par                                             on which banks and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par                                             markets are open for business \par                                             in Singapore. \par                                            "Fallback Provisions": Should \par                                             no USD/IDR reference rate appear \par                                             on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2 's website (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bi.go.id"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bi.go.id}}}\uc2 \f2 ), \par                                             Thomson Reuters Screen JISDOR \par                                             Page, or Bloomberg Page JISDOR, \par                                             or be otherwise made available \par                                             by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  (or its successor \par                                             as administrator) on the Fixing \par                                             Date, then the USD/IDR reference \par                                             rate for such Fixing Date shall \par                                             be determined by the Calculation \par                                             Agent by requesting quotations \par                                             for the mid USD/IDR spot \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                             exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate either (i) at or \par                                             about 11:00 a.m. Singapore time \par                                             on the first day (other than a \par                                             Saturday or a Sunday) following \par                                             the Fixing Date (if such day is \par                                             a Relevant Business Day) or (ii) \par                                             if the first day (other than a \par                                             Saturday or a Sunday) following \par                                             the Fixing Date is not a Relevant \par                                             Business Day, at or about 11:00 \par                                             a.m. Singapore time on the Fixing \par                                             Date from five banks active in \par                                             the USD/IDR \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign \par                                             exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets (such banks, \par                                             the "Reference Banks") as selected \par                                             by the Calculation Agent. \par                                            If five or four quotations are \par                                             provided as requested, the USD/IDR \par                                             reference rate will be the arithmetic \par                                             mean (rounded to the nearest whole \par                                             Rupiah, 0.5 being rounded upwards) \par                                             of the remaining three or two \par                                             such quotations, as the case may \par                                             be, for such rate provided by \par                                             the Reference Banks, after disregarding \par                                             the highest such quotation and \par                                             the lowest such quotation (provided \par                                             that, if two or more such quotations \par                                             are the highest such quotations, \par                                             then only one of such quotations \par                                             shall be disregarded, and if one \par                                             or more such quotations are the \par                                             lowest quotations, then only one \par                                             of such lowest quotations will \par                                             be disregarded). \par                                             If only three or two such quotations \par                                             are provided as requested, the \par                         