ses \par                                             related to the issuance of the \par                                             Notes. \par  6.     Codes: \par         (a) CUSIP:                         50207K9V5 \par         (b) ISIN:                          XS1106486936 \par         (c) Common Code:                   110648693 \par  7.     Identity of Dealer:                \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup Global Markets Limited\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par  8.     Identity of Calculation            Citibank, N.A. \par          Agent:                             Citigroup Centre \par                                             Canada Square \par                                             Canary Wharf \par                                             London E14 5LB \par                                             United Kingdom \par  \par                                             (acting through its Singapore \par                                             \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  derivatives trading group (or \par                                             any successor department/group)) \par  \par                                             In relation to the Fixing Date, \par                                             as soon as is reasonably practicable \par                                             after the determination of the \par                                             Applicable Rate in relation thereto, \par                                             on the date on which the relevant \par                                             Applicable Rate is to be determined \par                                             (or, if such date is not a Relevant \par                                             Business Day, then on the next \par                                             succeeding Relevant Business Day), \par                                             the Calculation Agent shall notify \par                                             the Issuer and the Global Agent \par                                             of the Applicable Rate, and the \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 16-10-14 1606GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                                             Interest Amount, and the Redemption \par                                             Amount or Early Redemption Amount, \par                                             as the case may be, in relation \par                                             thereto. \par                                            All determinations of the Calculation \par                                             Agent shall (in the absence of \par                                             manifest error) be final and binding \par                                             on all parties (including, but \par                                             not limited to, the Bank and the \par                                             Noteholders) and shall be made \par                                             in its sole discretion in good \par                                             faith and in a commercially reasonable \par                                             manner in accordance with a calculation \par                                             agent agreement between the Bank \par                                             and the Calculation Agent. \par  9.     Provision for Registered \par          Notes: \par         (a) Individual Definitive \par          Registered Notes Available         No \par          on Issue Date: \par         (b) DTC Global Note(s):            No \par         (c) Other Registered Global        Yes, issued in accordance with \par          Notes:                             the Global Agency Agreement, dated \par                                             January 8, 2001, among the Bank, \par                                             \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citibank, N.A\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., as Global Agent, \par                                             and the other parties thereto. \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 General Information\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Additional Information regarding the Notes\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1. The EU has adopted a Directive regarding the taxation of savings income (the "Savings Directive"). The Savings Directive requires Member States (as defined below) to provide to the tax authorities of other Member States details of payments of interest and other similar income paid by a person to an individual in another Member State, except that Austria and Luxembourg will instead impose a withholding system for a transitional period unless during such period they elect otherwise.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank undertakes that it will ensure that it maintains a paying agent in a country which is a member of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  (a "Member State") that will not be obliged to withhold or deduct tax pursuant to the Savings Directive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    2.         United States Federal Tax Matters \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The following supplements the discussion under the "Tax Matters" section of the Prospectus regarding the U.S. federal income tax treatment of the Notes, and is subject to the limitations and exceptions set forth therein. Any tax disclosure in the Prospectus or this pricing supplement is of a general nature only, is not exhaustive of all possible tax considerations and is not intended to be, and should not be construed to be, legal, business or tax advice to any particular prospective investor. Each prospective investor should consult its own tax advisor as to the particular tax consequences to it of the acquisition, ownership, and disposition of the Notes, including the effects of applicable U.S. federal, state, and local tax laws and non-U.S. tax laws and possible changes in tax laws.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Due to a change in law since the date of the Prospectus, the second paragraph of "-Payments of Interest" under the United States Holders section should be read as follows: "Interest paid by the Bank on the Notes constitutes income from sources outside the United States and will, depending on the circumstances, be "passive" or "general" income for purposes of computing the foreign tax credit."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Information with Respect to Foreign Financial Assets. Owners of "specified foreign financial assets" with an aggregate value in excess of $50,000 (and in some circumstances, a higher threshold) may be required to file an information report with respect to such assets with their tax returns. "Specified foreign financial assets" may include financial accounts maintained by foreign financial institutions (which may include the Notes), as well as the following, but only if they are not held in accounts maintained by financial institutions: (i) stocks and securities issued by non-United States persons, (ii) financial instruments and contracts held for investment that have non-United States issuers or counterparties, and (iii) interests in foreign entities. Holders are urged to consult their tax advisors regarding the application of this reporting obligation to their ownership of the Notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Medicare Tax. A U.S. holder that is an individual or estate, or a trust that does not fall into a special class of trusts that is exempt from such tax, will be subject to a 3.8% tax (the "Medicare tax") on the lesser of (1) the U.S. holder's "net investment income" for the relevant taxable year and (2) the excess of the U.S. holder's modified adjusted gross income for the taxable year over a certain threshold (which in the case of individuals will be between $125,000 and $250,000, depending on the individual's circumstances). A holder's net investment income will generally include its gross interest income and its net gains from the disposition of Notes, unless such interest payments or net gains are derived in the ordinary course of the conduct of a trade or business (other than a trade or business that consists of certain passive or trading activities). If you are a U.S. holder that is an individual, estate or trust, you are urged to consult your tax advisors regarding the applicability of the Medicare tax to your income and gains in respect of your investment in the Notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    3.         Additional Investment Considerations: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Notes offered by this Pricing Supplement are complex financial instruments and may not be suitable for certain investors. Investors intending to purchase the Notes should consult with their tax and financial advisors to ensure that the intended purchase meets the investment objective before making such purchase.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There are various risks associated with the Notes including, but not limited to, exchange rate risk, price risk and liquidity risk. Investors should consult with their own financial, legal and accounting advisors about the risks associated with an investment in these Notes, the appropriate tools to analyze that investment, and the suitability of the investment in each investor's particular circumstances. Holders of the Notes should also consult with their professional tax advisors regarding tax laws applicable to them.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Payment of each Interest Amount and the Redemption Amount will be based on the Applicable Rate, which is a measure of the rate of exchange between the Indonesian Rupiah and the USD. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates are volatile and will affect the holder's return. In addition, the government of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Indonesia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  can from time to time \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market. These \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or other governmental actions could adversely affect the value of the Notes, as well as the yield (in USD terms) on the Notes and the amount payable at maturity or upon acceleration. Even in the absence of governmental action directly affecting \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  exchange rates, political or economic developments in Indonesia or elsewhere could lead to significant and sudden changes in the exchange rate between the Indonesian Rupiah and the USD.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Indonesian Rupiah is an emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may be subject to particularly substantial volatility, as well as to government actions including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  controls, devaluations and other matters which could materially and adversely affect the value of the Notes.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The methodologies for determining the Applicable Rate may result in a Redemption Amount (or Early Redemption Amount, as the case may be) of the Notes, or an Interest Amount on the Notes, being significantly less than anticipated or less than what an alternative methodology for determining the IDR-USD exchange rate would yield.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 INTER-AMERICAN DEVELOPMENT BANK\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Name: Alberto L. Suria\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Title:    Chief Financial Officer and General Manager a.i., \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Finance Department\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 This information is provided by RNS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The company news service from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 London Stock Exchange\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 END\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 IODUNRNRSUARAAA [ 16-10-14 1606GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument RNS0000020141016eaag000vz\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \cl